window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b300-36f6fb3b8cc96bbd.json"]={sha256:"36f6fb3b8cc96bbd38d2efdb18e1cd4cb6a9df862e0982e3e68a619875a95901",value:{"id":"b300","title":"水利設施數位孿生","titleEn":"Digital twins for water infrastructure","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"以樟宜水再生廠數位孿生為真實入口，逐步建立從感測資料到決策證據的完整鏈結。十個單元分辨拓樸、時鐘、單位、校正與異常判讀的錯誤來源，並以原創小型算例驗證每項假設。課程把模型驗證與真實設備確認分開，讓學徒能指出預測可信的條件及仍需量測的疑問。","summaryEn":"Starting from the real Changi Water Reclamation Plant digital twin, build a chain from sensor records to decision evidence. Ten units distinguish topology, timing, units, calibration and anomaly interpretation through original numerical examples. Separate equation verification from physical validation and identify both the conditions supporting a prediction and questions requiring additional observations.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-coasts","subcategoryTitle":"海岸、港灣與水資源韌性","subcategoryTitleEn":"Coasts, ports and water-resource resilience","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-coasts","learningTags":["water","water-coasts","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-ecology","architectureNodes":[["感測資料與物件身分","Sensor data and asset identity"],["時間、單位與品質","Time, units and quality"],["守恆與可辨識模型","Conservation and identifiable models"],["獨立驗證與同化","Independent validation and assimilation"],["情境證據與審查","Scenario evidence and review"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[3,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-ecology","labels":["感測資料與物件身分","時間、單位與品質","守恆與可辨識模型","獨立驗證與同化","情境證據與審查"],"labelsEn":["Sensor data and asset identity","Time, units and quality","Conservation and identifiable models","Independent validation and assimilation","Scenario evidence and review"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"教學比較採用兩個不同的資料品質問題。首先，兩支獨立無偏水頭感測器分別為40±2 m與46±1 m，反變異數加權得到44.8 m；若兩者共同偏高3 m，融合結果也偏高3 m，原本較小的不確定度不能揭露共同偏差。其次，取壓點高程25 m與表壓水頭40 m相加得到65 m測壓管水頭。這兩個案例不互相交換數字，因為前者討論同一狀態的統計融合，後者討論單位和垂直基準。請分別保存原始讀值、假設與計算式，再說明增加哪一項獨立量測才能區分儀器偏差與模型誤差。","textEn":"Compare two distinct data-quality problems. Independent unbiased head measurements of 40±2 m and 46±1 m combine to 44.8 m by inverse-variance weighting. Adding a shared three-metre bias shifts that result by three metres; the nominal reduction in uncertainty does not expose common bias. Separately, a tap elevation of 25 m plus gauge pressure head 40 m yields piezometric head 65 m. Do not exchange numbers between these examples: one concerns statistical fusion of the same state, the other concerns units and vertical datum. Preserve raw values, assumptions and equations, then identify additional independent evidence needed to separate instrument bias from model error.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b300-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「網路拓樸與守恆殘差」與「時間同步與相位誤差」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Network topology and balance residuals\" and \"Time alignment and phase error\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b300-v15-01","title":"網路拓樸與守恆殘差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Network topology and balance residuals: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「網路拓樸與守恆殘差」如何影響水利設施數位孿生的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Network topology and balance residuals” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Digital twins for water infrastructure”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"數位孿生必須先知道每支感測器、管段與水池代表哪個物理物件，才能比較預測與觀測。節點流量依統一方向列入守恆式，蓄水變化另作一項，而不是把所有正值直接相加。水量殘差可能來自漏列支管、時間錯位、儀表偏移或真正漏水，因此單一殘差不能唯一辨識原因。建立穩定的資產識別碼與版本化連線表，能讓一次閥門改接與一次感測器更換在資料中保持可追溯，也能避免外觀相同的圖示遮蔽實際已改變的水路。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「網路拓樸與守恆殘差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A digital twin needs a physical identity for every sensor, pipe and tank before predictions can be compared with observations. Signed node flows enter a conservation equation, while changing storage remains a separate term. A residual can arise from an omitted branch, timing error, instrument bias or leakage and therefore does not identify its cause uniquely. Stable asset identifiers and versioned connections preserve the distinction between a changed water route and a replaced sensor, even when the displayed diagram looks unchanged. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Network topology and balance residuals” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設一個無蓄水節點，兩股入流為1.8及0.6 m³/s，量得出流2.3 m³/s；殘差r=1.8+0.6−2.3=0.1 m³/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Assume a storage-free teaching node with inflows 1.8 and 0.6 m³/s and measured outflow 2.3 m³/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「節點出現正水量殘差，就一定代表同等流量的管線漏水。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A positive node balance residual always equals the physical leakage flow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「網路拓樸與守恆殘差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Network topology and balance residuals”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-01-k1","title":"網路拓樸與守恆殘差","titleEn":"Network topology and balance residuals","text":"數位孿生必須先知道每支感測器、管段與水池代表哪個物理物件，才能比較預測與觀測。節點流量依統一方向列入守恆式，蓄水變化另作一項，而不是把所有正值直接相加。","textEn":"A digital twin needs a physical identity for every sensor, pipe and tank before predictions can be compared with observations. Signed node flows enter a conservation equation, while changing storage remains a separate term.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：節點出現正水量殘差，就一定代表同等流量的管線漏水。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A positive node balance residual always equals the physical leakage flow. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「網路拓樸與守恆殘差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Network topology and balance residuals\" is correct?","options":["節點出現正水量殘差，就一定代表同等流量的管線漏水。","數位孿生必須先知道每支感測器、管段與水池代表哪個物理物件，才能比較預測與觀測。","只要兩條曲線的相關係數最高，就證明兩個感測器已正確同步。"],"optionsEn":["A positive node balance residual always equals the physical leakage flow.","A digital twin needs a physical identity for every sensor, pipe and tank before predictions can be compared with observations.","Maximum correlation between two curves proves that their sensors are correctly synchronized."],"answer":1,"explanation":"數位孿生必須先知道每支感測器、管段與水池代表哪個物理物件，才能比較預測與觀測。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A digital twin needs a physical identity for every sensor, pipe and tank before predictions can be compared with observations. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b300-v15-02","title":"網路拓樸與守恆殘差：定量估算","titleEn":"Network topology and balance residuals: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「網路拓樸與守恆殘差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Network topology and balance residuals” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設一個無蓄水節點，兩股入流為1.8及0.6 m³/s，量得出流2.3 m³/s；殘差r=1.8+0.6−2.3=0.1 m³/s。此數值尚不能直接當作漏水量。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Assume a storage-free teaching node with inflows 1.8 and 0.6 m³/s and measured outflow 2.3 m³/s. Residual r=1.8+0.6−2.3=0.1 m³/s is not automatically a leakage estimate. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：逐一核對資產編號、流向符號、旁通管與量測時間，再以獨立水量計或水池水位變化驗算。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check asset identifiers, signs, bypasses and timestamps before using an independent meter or tank-level change to test balance.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設一個無蓄水節點，兩股入流為1.8及0.6 m³/s，量得出流2.3 m³/s；殘差r=1.8+0.6−2.3=0.1 m³/s。此數值尚不能直接當作漏水量。","textEn":"Assume a storage-free teaching node with inflows 1.8 and 0.6 m³/s and measured outflow 2.3 m³/s. Residual r=1.8+0.6−2.3=0.1 m³/s is not automatically a leakage estimate.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「網路拓樸與守恆殘差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Network topology and balance residuals\", which statement holds?","options":["把同一支感測器的資料複製十份再平均，就能得到十支獨立儀器的準確度。","把水力參數重新校正到量測曲線，就一定能消除任何時間步長造成的數值誤差。","教學假設一個無蓄水節點，兩股入流為1.8及0.6 m³/s，量得出流2.3 m³/s；殘差r=1.8+0.6−2.3=0.1 m³/s。"],"optionsEn":["Copying one sensor record ten times provides the accuracy of ten independent instruments.","Recalibrating hydraulic parameters always eliminates numerical error caused by the chosen time step.","Assume a storage-free teaching node with inflows 1.8 and 0.6 m³/s and measured outflow 2.3 m³/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設一個無蓄水節點，兩股入流為1.8及0.6 m³/s，量得出流2.3 m³/s；殘差r=1.8+0.6−2.3=0.1 m³/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Assume a storage-free teaching node with inflows 1.8 and 0.6 m³/s and measured outflow 2.3 m³/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b300-v15-03","title":"網路拓樸與守恆殘差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Network topology and balance residuals: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「網路拓樸與守恆殘差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Network topology and balance residuals” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"逐一核對資產編號、流向符號、旁通管與量測時間，再以獨立水量計或水池水位變化驗算。把改接前後的拓樸版本分開重播，觀察殘差是持續偏移還是只在切換期間出現，並保留校正紀錄以區分資料錯誤與真實水量缺口。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check asset identifiers, signs, bypasses and timestamps before using an independent meter or tank-level change to test balance. Replay topology versions separately and distinguish a persistent residual from a switching transient, retaining calibration records as evidence for competing explanations. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：繪出包含旁通管的四節點示意圖，先以正負號重算每點守恆，再故意漏列一段水路。比較所有節點殘差的空間分布，提出一項能區分漏列支管與儀表固定偏移的額外量測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw a four-node network with a bypass and calculate each signed balance. Omit one connection deliberately, compare the spatial residual pattern, and propose an additional measurement distinguishing that omission from fixed meter bias.","failure":"注意干擾：若旁通支管未納入模型，校正程序可能錯把少算的流量吸收到需求係數中。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An omitted bypass may be absorbed into calibrated demand coefficients. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐一核對資產編號、流向符號、旁通管與量測時間，再以獨立水量計或水池水位變化驗算。把改接前後的拓樸版本分開重播，觀察殘差是持續偏移還是只在切換期間出現，並保留校正紀錄以區分資料錯誤與真實水量缺口。","textEn":"Check asset identifiers, signs, bypasses and timestamps before using an independent meter or tank-level change to test balance. Replay topology versions separately and distinguish a persistent residual from a switching transient, retaining calibration records as evidence for competing explanations.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"繪出包含旁通管的四節點示意圖，先以正負號重算每點守恆，再故意漏列一段水路。比較所有節點殘差的空間分布，提出一項能區分漏列支管與儀表固定偏移的額外量測。","textEn":"Draw a four-node network with a bypass and calculate each signed balance. Omit one connection deliberately, compare the spatial residual pattern, and propose an additional measurement distinguishing that omission from fixed meter bias.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「網路拓樸與守恆殘差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Network topology and balance residuals\"?","options":["逐一核對資產編號、流向符號、旁通管與量測時間，再以獨立水量計或水池水位變化驗算。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","資料同化後的不確定度下降，就能證明原本的物理模型完全正確。"],"optionsEn":["Check asset identifiers, signs, bypasses and timestamps before using an independent meter or tank-level change to test balance.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Reduced uncertainty after assimilation proves that the underlying physical model is completely correct."],"answer":0,"explanation":"逐一核對資產編號、流向符號、旁通管與量測時間，再以獨立水量計或水池水位變化驗算。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check asset identifiers, signs, bypasses and timestamps before using an independent meter or tank-level change to test balance. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b300-v15-04","title":"網路拓樸與守恆殘差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Network topology and balance residuals: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「網路拓樸與守恆殘差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Network topology and balance residuals” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若旁通支管未納入模型，校正程序可能錯把少算的流量吸收到需求係數中。這會使平時殘差看似降低，卻在閥門切換後產生更大的偏差，不能用較小的訓練誤差證明拓樸正確。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An omitted bypass may be absorbed into calibrated demand coefficients. Training residuals then decrease while errors grow after valve changes, so a better fitted baseline does not demonstrate correct network connectivity. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：建立穩定的資產識別碼與版本化連線表，能讓一次閥門改接與一次感測器更換在資料中保持可追溯，也能避免外觀相同的圖示遮蔽實際已改變的水路。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Stable asset identifiers and versioned connections preserve the distinction between a changed water route and a replaced sensor, even when the displayed diagram looks unchanged.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「節點出現正水量殘差，就一定代表同等流量的管線漏水。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A positive node balance residual always equals the physical leakage flow.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若旁通支管未納入模型，校正程序可能錯把少算的流量吸收到需求係數中。這會使平時殘差看似降低，卻在閥門切換後產生更大的偏差，不能用較小的訓練誤差證明拓樸正確。","textEn":"An omitted bypass may be absorbed into calibrated demand coefficients. Training residuals then decrease while errors grow after valve changes, so a better fitted baseline does not demonstrate correct network connectivity.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「網路拓樸與守恆殘差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Network topology and balance residuals\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若旁通支管未納入模型，校正程序可能錯把少算的流量吸收到需求係數中。","只要兩條曲線的相關係數最高，就證明兩個感測器已正確同步。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","An omitted bypass may be absorbed into calibrated demand coefficients.","Maximum correlation between two curves proves that their sensors are correctly synchronized."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若旁通支管未納入模型，校正程序可能錯把少算的流量吸收到需求係數中。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An omitted bypass may be absorbed into calibrated demand coefficients. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b300-v15-05","title":"時間同步與相位誤差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Time alignment and phase error: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「時間同步與相位誤差」如何影響水利設施數位孿生的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Time alignment and phase error” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Digital twins for water infrastructure”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水位與流量紀錄常來自不同時鐘，資料到達伺服器的時間也可能晚於實際取樣。若直接以接收時間配對，正常的水力傳播便可能被誤認為設備故障。週期性訊號的固定時間差可換算成相位差，但只有在週期穩定時才有這種簡單關係；泵浦啟停的非週期事件要用事件時間和因果順序判讀。重採樣之前應保留原始時間戳、時區、品質旗標與取樣間隔，不能先把缺值平滑後再假設兩條曲線已同步。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「時間同步與相位誤差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Water levels and flows often come from different clocks, and arrival at a server can lag physical sampling. Pairing records by reception time may turn normal propagation into an apparent fault. A fixed delay maps to phase for a stable periodic signal, whereas irregular pump events require explicit event times and causal ordering. Preserve original timestamps, time zones, quality flags and sampling intervals before resampling; smoothing missing values does not establish synchronization between two records. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Time alignment and phase error” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設穩定週期T=900 s的水位振盪，一個通道晚記60 s；相位誤差φ=360×60/900=24°。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Assume a steady water-level period T=900 s and a channel timestamp delayed 60 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要兩條曲線的相關係數最高，就證明兩個感測器已正確同步。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Maximum correlation between two curves proves that their sensors are correctly synchronized.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「時間同步與相位誤差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Time alignment and phase error”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-05-k1","title":"時間同步與相位誤差","titleEn":"Time alignment and phase error","text":"水位與流量紀錄常來自不同時鐘，資料到達伺服器的時間也可能晚於實際取樣。若直接以接收時間配對，正常的水力傳播便可能被誤認為設備故障。","textEn":"Water levels and flows often come from different clocks, and arrival at a server can lag physical sampling. Pairing records by reception time may turn normal propagation into an apparent fault.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要兩條曲線的相關係數最高，就證明兩個感測器已正確同步。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Maximum correlation between two curves proves that their sensors are correctly synchronized. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「時間同步與相位誤差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Time alignment and phase error\" is correct?","options":["只要兩條曲線的相關係數最高，就證明兩個感測器已正確同步。","兩支壓力計讀值相同，就表示它們所在位置的總水頭必定相同。","水位與流量紀錄常來自不同時鐘，資料到達伺服器的時間也可能晚於實際取樣。"],"optionsEn":["Maximum correlation between two curves proves that their sensors are correctly synchronized.","Equal pressure readings always imply equal total hydraulic head at both locations.","Water levels and flows often come from different clocks, and arrival at a server can lag physical sampling."],"answer":2,"explanation":"水位與流量紀錄常來自不同時鐘，資料到達伺服器的時間也可能晚於實際取樣。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Water levels and flows often come from different clocks, and arrival at a server can lag physical sampling. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b300-v15-06","title":"時間同步與相位誤差：定量估算","titleEn":"Time alignment and phase error: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「時間同步與相位誤差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Time alignment and phase error” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設穩定週期T=900 s的水位振盪，一個通道晚記60 s；相位誤差φ=360×60/900=24°。此值不代表水在兩測站間真的旅行60 s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Assume a steady water-level period T=900 s and a channel timestamp delayed 60 s. Phase error φ=360×60/900=24°. This does not establish a physical travel time between stations. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以共同事件或獨立時鐘記錄檢查相對延遲，將取樣時間與接收時間分開繪圖。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check relative delay against a common event or independent clock, plotting sample and reception times separately.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設穩定週期T=900 s的水位振盪，一個通道晚記60 s；相位誤差φ=360×60/900=24°。此值不代表水在兩測站間真的旅行60 s。","textEn":"Assume a steady water-level period T=900 s and a channel timestamp delayed 60 s. Phase error φ=360×60/900=24°. This does not establish a physical travel time between stations.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「時間同步與相位誤差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Time alignment and phase error\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設穩定週期T=900 s的水位振盪，一個通道晚記60 s；相位誤差φ=360×60/900=24°。","最佳化程式只回傳一組參數，就證明這組參數已被資料唯一辨識。","驗證殘差的平均值是零，就表示模型的每一個預測值都完全準確。"],"optionsEn":["Assume a steady water-level period T=900 s and a channel timestamp delayed 60 s.","A single parameter vector returned by an optimizer proves unique identification by the data.","A zero mean validation residual means every individual model prediction is exact."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設穩定週期T=900 s的水位振盪，一個通道晚記60 s；相位誤差φ=360×60/900=24°。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Assume a steady water-level period T=900 s and a channel timestamp delayed 60 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b300-v15-07","title":"時間同步與相位誤差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Time alignment and phase error: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「時間同步與相位誤差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Time alignment and phase error” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以共同事件或獨立時鐘記錄檢查相對延遲，將取樣時間與接收時間分開繪圖。再測試延遲是否隨通訊負載變動；只有在時間校正可重現且不會倒置事件順序時，才比較模型的水力相位，並記錄重採樣所使用的方法。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check relative delay against a common event or independent clock, plotting sample and reception times separately. Test variation with communication load. Compare hydraulic phase only after reproducible time correction, preserving event order and documenting the resampling method used. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：建立一條十五分鐘週期的合成曲線與一條延後一分鐘的副本，再加入一次真正的水力延遲。分別標記時鐘偏移與傳播時間，說明僅靠相關係數為何無法辨認兩者，並寫出必要的獨立時間證據。","observationEn":"Site practice: Create a fifteen-minute synthetic cycle and a copy delayed one minute, then add genuine propagation delay. Label clock offset separately and explain why correlation alone cannot distinguish the causes, specifying the independent timing evidence required.","failure":"注意干擾：自動移動曲線以追求最高相關係數，可能把真實水力延遲一併消掉。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Shifting curves to maximize correlation can remove genuine hydraulic delay. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以共同事件或獨立時鐘記錄檢查相對延遲，將取樣時間與接收時間分開繪圖。再測試延遲是否隨通訊負載變動；只有在時間校正可重現且不會倒置事件順序時，才比較模型的水力相位，並記錄重採樣所使用的方法。","textEn":"Check relative delay against a common event or independent clock, plotting sample and reception times separately. Test variation with communication load. Compare hydraulic phase only after reproducible time correction, preserving event order and documenting the resampling method used.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"建立一條十五分鐘週期的合成曲線與一條延後一分鐘的副本，再加入一次真正的水力延遲。分別標記時鐘偏移與傳播時間，說明僅靠相關係數為何無法辨認兩者，並寫出必要的獨立時間證據。","textEn":"Create a fifteen-minute synthetic cycle and a copy delayed one minute, then add genuine propagation delay. Label clock offset separately and explain why correlation alone cannot distinguish the causes, specifying the independent timing evidence required.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「時間同步與相位誤差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Time alignment and phase error\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以共同事件或獨立時鐘記錄檢查相對延遲，將取樣時間與接收時間分開繪圖。","偵測器的真陽性率是百分之九十五，就表示每次警報都有百分之九十五機率是真的。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Check relative delay against a common event or independent clock, plotting sample and reception times separately.","A ninety-five-percent true-positive rate means every alert has a ninety-five-percent chance of being genuine."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以共同事件或獨立時鐘記錄檢查相對延遲，將取樣時間與接收時間分開繪圖。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check relative delay against a common event or independent clock, plotting sample and reception times separately. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b300-v15-08","title":"時間同步與相位誤差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Time alignment and phase error: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「時間同步與相位誤差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Time alignment and phase error” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"自動移動曲線以追求最高相關係數，可能把真實水力延遲一併消掉。若對所有通道套用同一補值規則，還可能製造本來不存在的同步尖峰，使異常分類器學到資料處理的痕跡。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Shifting curves to maximize correlation can remove genuine hydraulic delay. Applying one filling rule to every channel can also manufacture synchronized peaks, allowing an anomaly classifier to learn processing artifacts instead of physical behavior. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：重採樣之前應保留原始時間戳、時區、品質旗標與取樣間隔，不能先把缺值平滑後再假設兩條曲線已同步。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Preserve original timestamps, time zones, quality flags and sampling intervals before resampling; smoothing missing values does not establish synchronization between two records.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要兩條曲線的相關係數最高，就證明兩個感測器已正確同步。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Maximum correlation between two curves proves that their sensors are correctly synchronized.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"自動移動曲線以追求最高相關係數，可能把真實水力延遲一併消掉。若對所有通道套用同一補值規則，還可能製造本來不存在的同步尖峰，使異常分類器學到資料處理的痕跡。","textEn":"Shifting curves to maximize correlation can remove genuine hydraulic delay. Applying one filling rule to every channel can also manufacture synchronized peaks, allowing an anomaly classifier to learn processing artifacts instead of physical behavior.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「時間同步與相位誤差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Time alignment and phase error\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","兩支壓力計讀值相同，就表示它們所在位置的總水頭必定相同。","自動移動曲線以追求最高相關係數，可能把真實水力延遲一併消掉。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Equal pressure readings always imply equal total hydraulic head at both locations.","Shifting curves to maximize correlation can remove genuine hydraulic delay."],"answer":2,"explanation":"自動移動曲線以追求最高相關係數，可能把真實水力延遲一併消掉。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Shifting curves to maximize correlation can remove genuine hydraulic delay. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b300-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「單位、基準面與壓力水頭」與「獨立感測器的加權融合」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Units, datums and pressure head\" and \"Weighted fusion of independent sensors\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b300-v15-09","title":"單位、基準面與壓力水頭：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Units, datums and pressure head: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「單位、基準面與壓力水頭」如何影響水利設施數位孿生的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Units, datums and pressure head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Digital twins for water infrastructure”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"數位孿生交換資料時，壓力、壓力水頭與總水頭必須明確區分。相同壓力讀值裝在不同高程，代表的測壓管水頭並不相同；若使用總能量水頭，還要說明速度水頭是否納入。感測器可能回報表壓或絕對壓力，地形資料也可能使用不同垂直基準面，因此欄位名稱相同仍不足以證明可以相減。將量綱、密度假設、垂直基準與感測器取壓位置一起版本化，才有可能在設備更換後重現同一個物理判讀。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「單位、基準面與壓力水頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Data exchange must distinguish pressure, pressure head and total head. Equal pressure readings at different elevations do not imply equal piezometric head; total energy head also requires a stated velocity contribution. Instruments may report gauge or absolute pressure, while terrain records may use different vertical datums. Matching column names are therefore insufficient. Version the units, assumed density, elevation datum and pressure-tap position together so that replacing an instrument does not silently change the physical interpretation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Units, datums and pressure head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設淡水ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²，表壓水頭40 m與取壓點高程25 m；表壓p=392.4 kPa，測壓管水頭H=25+40=65 m，未含速度水頭。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Assume freshwater density 1000 kg/m³, g=9.81 m/s², gauge pressure head 40 m and tap elevation 25 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩支壓力計讀值相同，就表示它們所在位置的總水頭必定相同。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal pressure readings always imply equal total hydraulic head at both locations.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「單位、基準面與壓力水頭」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Units, datums and pressure head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-09-k1","title":"單位、基準面與壓力水頭","titleEn":"Units, datums and pressure head","text":"數位孿生交換資料時，壓力、壓力水頭與總水頭必須明確區分。相同壓力讀值裝在不同高程，代表的測壓管水頭並不相同；若使用總能量水頭，還要說明速度水頭是否納入。","textEn":"Data exchange must distinguish pressure, pressure head and total head. Equal pressure readings at different elevations do not imply equal piezometric head; total energy head also requires a stated velocity contribution.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩支壓力計讀值相同，就表示它們所在位置的總水頭必定相同。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal pressure readings always imply equal total hydraulic head at both locations. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「單位、基準面與壓力水頭」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Units, datums and pressure head\" is correct?","options":["數位孿生交換資料時，壓力、壓力水頭與總水頭必須明確區分。","兩支壓力計讀值相同，就表示它們所在位置的總水頭必定相同。","把同一支感測器的資料複製十份再平均，就能得到十支獨立儀器的準確度。"],"optionsEn":["Data exchange must distinguish pressure, pressure head and total head.","Equal pressure readings always imply equal total hydraulic head at both locations.","Copying one sensor record ten times provides the accuracy of ten independent instruments."],"answer":0,"explanation":"數位孿生交換資料時，壓力、壓力水頭與總水頭必須明確區分。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Data exchange must distinguish pressure, pressure head and total head. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b300-v15-10","title":"單位、基準面與壓力水頭：定量估算","titleEn":"Units, datums and pressure head: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「單位、基準面與壓力水頭」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Units, datums and pressure head” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設淡水ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²，表壓水頭40 m與取壓點高程25 m；表壓p=392.4 kPa，測壓管水頭H=25+40=65 m，未含速度水頭。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Assume freshwater density 1000 kg/m³, g=9.81 m/s², gauge pressure head 40 m and tap elevation 25 m. Gauge pressure is 392.4 kPa and piezometric head H=65 m, excluding velocity head. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先用一筆可手算的固定數值逐層通過資料介面，確認公斤帕與帕的倍率以及公尺的垂直基準。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Pass one hand-checkable value through every interface to verify pressure scaling and elevation datum.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設淡水ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²，表壓水頭40 m與取壓點高程25 m；表壓p=392.4 kPa，測壓管水頭H=25+40=65 m，未含速度水頭。","textEn":"Assume freshwater density 1000 kg/m³, g=9.81 m/s², gauge pressure head 40 m and tap elevation 25 m. Gauge pressure is 392.4 kPa and piezometric head H=65 m, excluding velocity head.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「單位、基準面與壓力水頭」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Units, datums and pressure head\", which statement holds?","options":["把水力參數重新校正到量測曲線，就一定能消除任何時間步長造成的數值誤差。","教學假設淡水ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²，表壓水頭40 m與取壓點高程25 m。","資料同化後的不確定度下降，就能證明原本的物理模型完全正確。"],"optionsEn":["Recalibrating hydraulic parameters always eliminates numerical error caused by the chosen time step.","Assume freshwater density 1000 kg/m³, g=9.81 m/s², gauge pressure head 40 m and tap elevation 25 m.","Reduced uncertainty after assimilation proves that the underlying physical model is completely correct."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設淡水ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²，表壓水頭40 m與取壓點高程25 m；表壓p=392.4 kPa，測壓管水頭H=25+40=65 m，未含速度水頭。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Assume freshwater density 1000 kg/m³, g=9.81 m/s², gauge pressure head 40 m and tap elevation 25 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b300-v15-11","title":"單位、基準面與壓力水頭：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Units, datums and pressure head: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「單位、基準面與壓力水頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Units, datums and pressure head” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先用一筆可手算的固定數值逐層通過資料介面，確認公斤帕與帕的倍率以及公尺的垂直基準。將感測器零點、取壓口高程和大氣壓處理方式列入資料字典，再對照獨立水準測量，不以圖上的數字相近作為基準一致的證據。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Pass one hand-checkable value through every interface to verify pressure scaling and elevation datum. Document instrument zero, tap elevation and atmospheric-pressure treatment, then compare an independent level survey instead of treating similar displayed numbers as evidence of datum consistency. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：建立表壓、絕對壓力、壓力水頭與測壓管水頭四欄對照表，逐欄標出單位與基準。故意將其中一欄改成千帕，設計一個能在資料進入模型前即拒絕錯誤倍率的檢核條件。","observationEn":"Site practice: Build a table separating gauge pressure, absolute pressure, pressure head and piezometric head with units and datums. Change one column to kilopascals and design a validation rule that rejects incorrect scaling before model ingestion.","failure":"注意干擾：若模型把絕對壓力當成表壓，會加入一個近似大氣壓的假水頭；若又用需求校正抵消此差，模型可能在另一海拔或天氣條件下失準。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating absolute pressure as gauge pressure introduces a spurious atmospheric head. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先用一筆可手算的固定數值逐層通過資料介面，確認公斤帕與帕的倍率以及公尺的垂直基準。將感測器零點、取壓口高程和大氣壓處理方式列入資料字典，再對照獨立水準測量，不以圖上的數字相近作為基準一致的證據。","textEn":"Pass one hand-checkable value through every interface to verify pressure scaling and elevation datum. Document instrument zero, tap elevation and atmospheric-pressure treatment, then compare an independent level survey instead of treating similar displayed numbers as evidence of datum consistency.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"建立表壓、絕對壓力、壓力水頭與測壓管水頭四欄對照表，逐欄標出單位與基準。故意將其中一欄改成千帕，設計一個能在資料進入模型前即拒絕錯誤倍率的檢核條件。","textEn":"Build a table separating gauge pressure, absolute pressure, pressure head and piezometric head with units and datums. Change one column to kilopascals and design a validation rule that rejects incorrect scaling before model ingestion.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「單位、基準面與壓力水頭」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Units, datums and pressure head\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","只要數位孿生預測某方案耗能較低，就可以忽略供水限制直接執行。","先用一筆可手算的固定數值逐層通過資料介面，確認公斤帕與帕的倍率以及公尺的垂直基準。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Any strategy predicted to use less energy can be implemented without checking water-service constraints.","Pass one hand-checkable value through every interface to verify pressure scaling and elevation datum."],"answer":2,"explanation":"先用一筆可手算的固定數值逐層通過資料介面，確認公斤帕與帕的倍率以及公尺的垂直基準。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Pass one hand-checkable value through every interface to verify pressure scaling and elevation datum. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b300-v15-12","title":"單位、基準面與壓力水頭：失效診斷","titleEn":"Units, datums and pressure head: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「單位、基準面與壓力水頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Units, datums and pressure head” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若模型把絕對壓力當成表壓，會加入一個近似大氣壓的假水頭；若又用需求校正抵消此差，模型可能在另一海拔或天氣條件下失準。單位錯誤不應交給參數最佳化掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating absolute pressure as gauge pressure introduces a spurious atmospheric head. Calibration may conceal it temporarily, then fail at another elevation or atmospheric condition; parameter optimization should not mask unit or datum errors. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：將量綱、密度假設、垂直基準與感測器取壓位置一起版本化，才有可能在設備更換後重現同一個物理判讀。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Version the units, assumed density, elevation datum and pressure-tap position together so that replacing an instrument does not silently change the physical interpretation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩支壓力計讀值相同，就表示它們所在位置的總水頭必定相同。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal pressure readings always imply equal total hydraulic head at both locations.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若模型把絕對壓力當成表壓，會加入一個近似大氣壓的假水頭；若又用需求校正抵消此差，模型可能在另一海拔或天氣條件下失準。單位錯誤不應交給參數最佳化掩蓋。","textEn":"Treating absolute pressure as gauge pressure introduces a spurious atmospheric head. Calibration may conceal it temporarily, then fail at another elevation or atmospheric condition; parameter optimization should not mask unit or datum errors.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「單位、基準面與壓力水頭」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Units, datums and pressure head\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若模型把絕對壓力當成表壓，會加入一個近似大氣壓的假水頭；若又用需求校正抵消此差，模型可能在另一海拔或天氣條件下失準。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","把同一支感測器的資料複製十份再平均，就能得到十支獨立儀器的準確度。"],"optionsEn":["Treating absolute pressure as gauge pressure introduces a spurious atmospheric head.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Copying one sensor record ten times provides the accuracy of ten independent instruments."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若模型把絕對壓力當成表壓，會加入一個近似大氣壓的假水頭；若又用需求校正抵消此差，模型可能在另一海拔或天氣條件下失準。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating absolute pressure as gauge pressure introduces a spurious atmospheric head. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b300-v15-13","title":"獨立感測器的加權融合：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Weighted fusion of independent sensors: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「獨立感測器的加權融合」如何影響水利設施數位孿生的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Weighted fusion of independent sensors” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Digital twins for water infrastructure”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"兩支感測器估計同一個量時，若誤差無偏、互相獨立而且變異數已知，可使用反變異數加權得到較小的不確定度。權重不是儀器價格、顯示小數位數或資料筆數的替代說法，而是對誤差模型的明確假設。兩支儀器若共用取壓管、供電或校正來源，可能具有共同偏差，此時獨立公式會過度樂觀。融合之前要確認兩者真的觀察同一物理狀態，同時保留各自原始值，才能在融合結果看似平穩時發現單一通道漂移。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「獨立感測器的加權融合」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"For two estimates of the same quantity, inverse-variance weighting reduces uncertainty when errors are unbiased, independent and have known variances. Weight is not a proxy for instrument price, displayed precision or record count. Shared pressure lines, power supplies or calibration references can introduce common bias, making the independence formula optimistic. Confirm that both instruments observe the same physical state and preserve their separate records so that a stable fused estimate does not conceal one drifting channel. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Weighted fusion of independent sensors” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設兩個獨立無偏水頭估計40±2 m與46±1 m，其中±為標準不確定度；融合值=(40/4+46/1)/(1/4+1)=44.8 m，標準不確定度√(1/1.25)=0.8944 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Assume independent unbiased head estimates 40±2 m and 46±1 m, with standard uncertainties.","failure":"常見誤解：「把同一支感測器的資料複製十份再平均，就能得到十支獨立儀器的準確度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Copying one sensor record ten times provides the accuracy of ten independent instruments.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「獨立感測器的加權融合」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Weighted fusion of independent sensors”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-13-k1","title":"獨立感測器的加權融合","titleEn":"Weighted fusion of independent sensors","text":"兩支感測器估計同一個量時，若誤差無偏、互相獨立而且變異數已知，可使用反變異數加權得到較小的不確定度。權重不是儀器價格、顯示小數位數或資料筆數的替代說法，而是對誤差模型的明確假設。","textEn":"For two estimates of the same quantity, inverse-variance weighting reduces uncertainty when errors are unbiased, independent and have known variances. Weight is not a proxy for instrument price, displayed precision or record count.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：把同一支感測器的資料複製十份再平均，就能得到十支獨立儀器的準確度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Copying one sensor record ten times provides the accuracy of ten independent instruments. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「獨立感測器的加權融合」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Weighted fusion of independent sensors\" is correct?","options":["把同一支感測器的資料複製十份再平均，就能得到十支獨立儀器的準確度。","兩支感測器估計同一個量時，若誤差無偏、互相獨立而且變異數已知，可使用反變異數加權得到較小的不確定度。","最佳化程式只回傳一組參數，就證明這組參數已被資料唯一辨識。"],"optionsEn":["Copying one sensor record ten times provides the accuracy of ten independent instruments.","For two estimates of the same quantity, inverse-variance weighting reduces uncertainty when errors are unbiased, independent and have known variances.","A single parameter vector returned by an optimizer proves unique identification by the data."],"answer":1,"explanation":"兩支感測器估計同一個量時，若誤差無偏、互相獨立而且變異數已知，可使用反變異數加權得到較小的不確定度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"For two estimates of the same quantity, inverse-variance weighting reduces uncertainty when errors are unbiased, independent and have known variances. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b300-v15-14","title":"獨立感測器的加權融合：定量估算","titleEn":"Weighted fusion of independent sensors: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「獨立感測器的加權融合」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Weighted fusion of independent sensors” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設兩個獨立無偏水頭估計40±2 m與46±1 m，其中±為標準不確定度；融合值=(40/4+46/1)/(1/4+1)=44.8 m，標準不確定度√(1/1.25)=0.8944 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Assume independent unbiased head estimates 40±2 m and 46±1 m, with standard uncertainties. The fused estimate is (40/4+46)/(1/4+1)=44.8 m, with standard uncertainty √(1/1.25)=0.8944 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先檢查校正與安裝是否提供獨立性證據，再用並行資料估計殘差相關性。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check calibration and installation evidence for independence, then estimate residual correlation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設兩個獨立無偏水頭估計40±2 m與46±1 m，其中±為標準不確定度；融合值=(40/4+46/1)/(1/4+1)=44.8 m，標準不確定度√(1/1.25)=0.8944 m。","textEn":"Assume independent unbiased head estimates 40±2 m and 46±1 m, with standard uncertainties. The fused estimate is (40/4+46)/(1/4+1)=44.8 m, with standard uncertainty √(1/1.25)=0.8944 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「獨立感測器的加權融合」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Weighted fusion of independent sensors\", which statement holds?","options":["驗證殘差的平均值是零，就表示模型的每一個預測值都完全準確。","偵測器的真陽性率是百分之九十五，就表示每次警報都有百分之九十五機率是真的。","教學假設兩個獨立無偏水頭估計40±2 m與46±1 m，其中±為標準不確定度。"],"optionsEn":["A zero mean validation residual means every individual model prediction is exact.","A ninety-five-percent true-positive rate means every alert has a ninety-five-percent chance of being genuine.","Assume independent unbiased head estimates 40±2 m and 46±1 m, with standard uncertainties."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設兩個獨立無偏水頭估計40±2 m與46±1 m，其中±為標準不確定度；融合值=(40/4+46/1)/(1/4+1)=44.8 m，標準不確定度√(1/1.25)=0.8944 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Assume independent unbiased head estimates 40±2 m and 46±1 m, with standard uncertainties. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b300-v15-15","title":"獨立感測器的加權融合：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Weighted fusion of independent sensors: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「獨立感測器的加權融合」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Weighted fusion of independent sensors” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先檢查校正與安裝是否提供獨立性證據，再用並行資料估計殘差相關性。以已知參考值分別評估兩支感測器的偏差，並比較融合前後的區間涵蓋率；若共同誤差存在，應在協方差中明列，而非再加入第三支相同來源儀器就宣稱問題解決。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check calibration and installation evidence for independence, then estimate residual correlation. Compare each sensor with an external reference and evaluate interval coverage before and after fusion. Represent shared error in covariance instead of assuming another similarly sourced sensor eliminates the problem. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算兩支感測器等權平均與反變異數平均，說明結果為何偏向較小變異數者。再替兩者加入相同的三公尺偏移，觀察融合值與原公式不確定度的變化，指出原先獨立無偏假設何處失效。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare equal-weight and inverse-variance estimates, then add the same three-metre bias to both sensors. Recompute the fused value and nominal uncertainty, explaining which independence or unbiasedness assumptions no longer describe the changed data.","failure":"注意干擾：若把重複上傳的同一筆量測視為多支獨立感測器，計算會顯示不確定度不斷下降，實際資訊卻沒有增加。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Counting repeated uploads as independent sensors artificially reduces calculated uncertainty without adding information. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先檢查校正與安裝是否提供獨立性證據，再用並行資料估計殘差相關性。以已知參考值分別評估兩支感測器的偏差，並比較融合前後的區間涵蓋率；若共同誤差存在，應在協方差中明列，而非再加入第三支相同來源儀器就宣稱問題解決。","textEn":"Check calibration and installation evidence for independence, then estimate residual correlation. Compare each sensor with an external reference and evaluate interval coverage before and after fusion. Represent shared error in covariance instead of assuming another similarly sourced sensor eliminates the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算兩支感測器等權平均與反變異數平均，說明結果為何偏向較小變異數者。再替兩者加入相同的三公尺偏移，觀察融合值與原公式不確定度的變化，指出原先獨立無偏假設何處失效。","textEn":"Compare equal-weight and inverse-variance estimates, then add the same three-metre bias to both sensors. Recompute the fused value and nominal uncertainty, explaining which independence or unbiasedness assumptions no longer describe the changed data.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「獨立感測器的加權融合」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Weighted fusion of independent sensors\"?","options":["先檢查校正與安裝是否提供獨立性證據，再用並行資料估計殘差相關性。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","節點出現正水量殘差，就一定代表同等流量的管線漏水。"],"optionsEn":["Check calibration and installation evidence for independence, then estimate residual correlation.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A positive node balance residual always equals the physical leakage flow."],"answer":0,"explanation":"先檢查校正與安裝是否提供獨立性證據，再用並行資料估計殘差相關性。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check calibration and installation evidence for independence, then estimate residual correlation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b300-v15-16","title":"獨立感測器的加權融合：失效診斷","titleEn":"Weighted fusion of independent sensors: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「獨立感測器的加權融合」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Weighted fusion of independent sensors” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若把重複上傳的同一筆量測視為多支獨立感測器，計算會顯示不確定度不斷下降，實際資訊卻沒有增加。共用錯誤基準的儀器也可能彼此吻合而一起偏離真值，因此一致性不等於準確性。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Counting repeated uploads as independent sensors artificially reduces calculated uncertainty without adding information. Instruments sharing an incorrect reference can agree closely while all departing from the true value, so agreement is not equivalent to accuracy. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：融合之前要確認兩者真的觀察同一物理狀態，同時保留各自原始值，才能在融合結果看似平穩時發現單一通道漂移。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Confirm that both instruments observe the same physical state and preserve their separate records so that a stable fused estimate does not conceal one drifting channel.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「把同一支感測器的資料複製十份再平均，就能得到十支獨立儀器的準確度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Copying one sensor record ten times provides the accuracy of ten independent instruments.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若把重複上傳的同一筆量測視為多支獨立感測器，計算會顯示不確定度不斷下降，實際資訊卻沒有增加。共用錯誤基準的儀器也可能彼此吻合而一起偏離真值，因此一致性不等於準確性。","textEn":"Counting repeated uploads as independent sensors artificially reduces calculated uncertainty without adding information. Instruments sharing an incorrect reference can agree closely while all departing from the true value, so agreement is not equivalent to accuracy.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「獨立感測器的加權融合」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Weighted fusion of independent sensors\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","若把重複上傳的同一筆量測視為多支獨立感測器，計算會顯示不確定度不斷下降，實際資訊卻沒有增加。","最佳化程式只回傳一組參數，就證明這組參數已被資料唯一辨識。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Counting repeated uploads as independent sensors artificially reduces calculated uncertainty without adding information.","A single parameter vector returned by an optimizer proves unique identification by the data."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若把重複上傳的同一筆量測視為多支獨立感測器，計算會顯示不確定度不斷下降，實際資訊卻沒有增加。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Counting repeated uploads as independent sensors artificially reduces calculated uncertainty without adding information. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b300-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「參數可辨識性與校正實驗」與「時間步長與數值守恆」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Parameter identifiability and calibration experiments\" and \"Time steps and numerical conservation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b300-v15-17","title":"參數可辨識性與校正實驗：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Parameter identifiability and calibration experiments: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「參數可辨識性與校正實驗」如何影響水利設施數位孿生的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Parameter identifiability and calibration experiments” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Digital twins for water infrastructure”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"模型參數能被最佳化程式找到一組數值，不代表資料足以唯一辨識它們。不同粗糙度、需求分配或感測器偏差可能形成相似的壓力殘差，讓多組參數都看似符合觀測。局部敏感度矩陣的獨立欄位代表不同參數會留下可分辨的影響；若欄位近乎平行，量測噪音就會造成巨大的參數變動。校正實驗應改變可控制的工況或增加不同位置量測，並保留參數合理範圍，不能只靠增加同一工況的重複資料期待問題自動消失。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「參數可辨識性與校正實驗」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Finding a parameter vector does not mean observations identify it uniquely. Roughness, demand distribution and sensor bias can produce similar pressure residuals, allowing many apparently successful fits. Independent columns of a local sensitivity matrix indicate distinguishable parameter effects; nearly parallel columns amplify observation noise into large parameter changes. Calibration should introduce different operating conditions or observation locations and retain plausible parameter ranges, rather than expecting repeated measurements under one unchanged condition to resolve the ambiguity. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Parameter identifiability and calibration experiments” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學線性模型以無因次參數r與d表示，只有r+d=8時，(3,5)與(4,4)都符合。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: In a dimensionless teaching model, r+d=8 admits both (3,5) and (4,4).","failure":"常見誤解：「最佳化程式只回傳一組參數，就證明這組參數已被資料唯一辨識。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A single parameter vector returned by an optimizer proves unique identification by the data.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「參數可辨識性與校正實驗」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Parameter identifiability and calibration experiments”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-17-k1","title":"參數可辨識性與校正實驗","titleEn":"Parameter identifiability and calibration experiments","text":"模型參數能被最佳化程式找到一組數值，不代表資料足以唯一辨識它們。不同粗糙度、需求分配或感測器偏差可能形成相似的壓力殘差，讓多組參數都看似符合觀測。","textEn":"Finding a parameter vector does not mean observations identify it uniquely. Roughness, demand distribution and sensor bias can produce similar pressure residuals, allowing many apparently successful fits.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：最佳化程式只回傳一組參數，就證明這組參數已被資料唯一辨識。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A single parameter vector returned by an optimizer proves unique identification by the data. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「參數可辨識性與校正實驗」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Parameter identifiability and calibration experiments\" is correct?","options":["最佳化程式只回傳一組參數，就證明這組參數已被資料唯一辨識。","把水力參數重新校正到量測曲線，就一定能消除任何時間步長造成的數值誤差。","模型參數能被最佳化程式找到一組數值，不代表資料足以唯一辨識它們。"],"optionsEn":["A single parameter vector returned by an optimizer proves unique identification by the data.","Recalibrating hydraulic parameters always eliminates numerical error caused by the chosen time step.","Finding a parameter vector does not mean observations identify it uniquely."],"answer":2,"explanation":"模型參數能被最佳化程式找到一組數值，不代表資料足以唯一辨識它們。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Finding a parameter vector does not mean observations identify it uniquely. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b300-v15-18","title":"參數可辨識性與校正實驗：定量估算","titleEn":"Parameter identifiability and calibration experiments: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「參數可辨識性與校正實驗」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Parameter identifiability and calibration experiments” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學線性模型以無因次參數r與d表示，只有r+d=8時，(3,5)與(4,4)都符合。增加獨立觀測r+2d=13後，矩陣行列式為1，解得r=3、d=5；此僅為可辨識性示例。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: In a dimensionless teaching model, r+d=8 admits both (3,5) and (4,4). Adding r+2d=13 gives matrix determinant 1 and identifies r=3, d=5; this is an identifiability example, not a field calibration. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以多組起始參數重跑校正，檢查是否得到相似誤差卻不同的參數。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Repeat calibration from several initial values and look for similar residuals with different parameters.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學線性模型以無因次參數r與d表示，只有r+d=8時，(3,5)與(4,4)都符合。增加獨立觀測r+2d=13後，矩陣行列式為1，解得r=3、d=5；此僅為可辨識性示例。","textEn":"In a dimensionless teaching model, r+d=8 admits both (3,5) and (4,4). Adding r+2d=13 gives matrix determinant 1 and identifies r=3, d=5; this is an identifiability example, not a field calibration.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「參數可辨識性與校正實驗」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Parameter identifiability and calibration experiments\", which statement holds?","options":["教學線性模型以無因次參數r與d表示，只有r+d=8時，(3,5)與(4,4)都符合。","資料同化後的不確定度下降，就能證明原本的物理模型完全正確。","只要數位孿生預測某方案耗能較低，就可以忽略供水限制直接執行。"],"optionsEn":["In a dimensionless teaching model, r+d=8 admits both (3,5) and (4,4).","Reduced uncertainty after assimilation proves that the underlying physical model is completely correct.","Any strategy predicted to use less energy can be implemented without checking water-service constraints."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學線性模型以無因次參數r與d表示，只有r+d=8時，(3,5)與(4,4)都符合。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"In a dimensionless teaching model, r+d=8 admits both (3,5) and (4,4). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b300-v15-19","title":"參數可辨識性與校正實驗：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Parameter identifiability and calibration experiments: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「參數可辨識性與校正實驗」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Parameter identifiability and calibration experiments” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以多組起始參數重跑校正，檢查是否得到相似誤差卻不同的參數。列出敏感度矩陣及其尺度，測試新增量測能否提供不同方向的資訊，再用未參與校正的工況驗證；即使矩陣可逆，也應分析量測噪音對解的放大程度。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Repeat calibration from several initial values and look for similar residuals with different parameters. Inspect scaled sensitivities, test whether added measurements provide independent information, and validate under held-out conditions. Invertibility alone does not establish acceptable sensitivity to measurement noise. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫出兩條教學線性觀測方程的交點，再把第二條改為2r+2d=16。比較新增資料前後的解集合，說明多一條方程為何不一定多一項獨立資訊，並提出不同工況下的第三個觀測構想。","observationEn":"Site practice: Plot the two teaching equations, then replace the second with 2r+2d=16. Compare solution sets and explain why another equation may add no independent information, proposing a third observation under a genuinely different condition.","failure":"注意干擾：強制最佳化器輸出唯一結果，可能只是演算法選了眾多等價解之一。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A unique optimizer output may merely select one of many equivalent solutions. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以多組起始參數重跑校正，檢查是否得到相似誤差卻不同的參數。列出敏感度矩陣及其尺度，測試新增量測能否提供不同方向的資訊，再用未參與校正的工況驗證；即使矩陣可逆，也應分析量測噪音對解的放大程度。","textEn":"Repeat calibration from several initial values and look for similar residuals with different parameters. Inspect scaled sensitivities, test whether added measurements provide independent information, and validate under held-out conditions. Invertibility alone does not establish acceptable sensitivity to measurement noise.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫出兩條教學線性觀測方程的交點，再把第二條改為2r+2d=16。比較新增資料前後的解集合，說明多一條方程為何不一定多一項獨立資訊，並提出不同工況下的第三個觀測構想。","textEn":"Plot the two teaching equations, then replace the second with 2r+2d=16. Compare solution sets and explain why another equation may add no independent information, proposing a third observation under a genuinely different condition.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「參數可辨識性與校正實驗」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Parameter identifiability and calibration experiments\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","以多組起始參數重跑校正，檢查是否得到相似誤差卻不同的參數。","只要兩條曲線的相關係數最高，就證明兩個感測器已正確同步。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Repeat calibration from several initial values and look for similar residuals with different parameters.","Maximum correlation between two curves proves that their sensors are correctly synchronized."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以多組起始參數重跑校正，檢查是否得到相似誤差卻不同的參數。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Repeat calibration from several initial values and look for similar residuals with different parameters. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b300-v15-20","title":"參數可辨識性與校正實驗：失效診斷","titleEn":"Parameter identifiability and calibration experiments: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「參數可辨識性與校正實驗」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Parameter identifiability and calibration experiments” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"強制最佳化器輸出唯一結果，可能只是演算法選了眾多等價解之一。若參數走到邊界卻仍有系統殘差，應先檢查模型結構與資料偏差，而非擴大到不合理的物理範圍繼續追求低誤差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A unique optimizer output may merely select one of many equivalent solutions. Parameters stuck at bounds with systematic residuals should trigger checks of model structure and data bias, rather than unrestricted expansion into physically implausible ranges. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：校正實驗應改變可控制的工況或增加不同位置量測，並保留參數合理範圍，不能只靠增加同一工況的重複資料期待問題自動消失。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Calibration should introduce different operating conditions or observation locations and retain plausible parameter ranges, rather than expecting repeated measurements under one unchanged condition to resolve the ambiguity.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「最佳化程式只回傳一組參數，就證明這組參數已被資料唯一辨識。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A single parameter vector returned by an optimizer proves unique identification by the data.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"強制最佳化器輸出唯一結果，可能只是演算法選了眾多等價解之一。若參數走到邊界卻仍有系統殘差，應先檢查模型結構與資料偏差，而非擴大到不合理的物理範圍繼續追求低誤差。","textEn":"A unique optimizer output may merely select one of many equivalent solutions. Parameters stuck at bounds with systematic residuals should trigger checks of model structure and data bias, rather than unrestricted expansion into physically implausible ranges.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「參數可辨識性與校正實驗」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Parameter identifiability and calibration experiments\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","把水力參數重新校正到量測曲線，就一定能消除任何時間步長造成的數值誤差。","強制最佳化器輸出唯一結果，可能只是演算法選了眾多等價解之一。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Recalibrating hydraulic parameters always eliminates numerical error caused by the chosen time step.","A unique optimizer output may merely select one of many equivalent solutions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"強制最佳化器輸出唯一結果，可能只是演算法選了眾多等價解之一。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A unique optimizer output may merely select one of many equivalent solutions. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b300-v15-21","title":"時間步長與數值守恆：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Time steps and numerical conservation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「時間步長與數值守恆」如何影響水利設施數位孿生的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Time steps and numerical conservation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Digital twins for water infrastructure”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"動態水量模型將連續的入流與出流積分成蓄水變化，有限時間步長會引入離散誤差。若入流在步內快速增加，使用步首值會低估水量；縮短步長通常有助於比較收斂，但不能修正漏掉的水路或錯誤的邊界。模型驗證需分清楚程式是否解對所選方程，以及方程是否描述真實設備。對已知解析解的合成案例先做數值驗證，再以不同步長比較水量閉合，可避免把演算法誤差當成需要重新校正的水力參數。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「時間步長與數值守恆」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A dynamic balance integrates changing inflow and outflow into storage, and finite time steps introduce discretization error. Using the initial inflow underestimates volume during a rising interval. Smaller steps support convergence checks but cannot repair omitted pathways or wrong boundaries. Distinguish solving the chosen equations correctly from choosing equations that describe the plant. Start with synthetic cases having analytical solutions, then compare balance closure across time steps so that numerical error is not absorbed into calibrated hydraulic parameters. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Time steps and numerical conservation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設60 s內入流Q(t)=10+0.1t m³/s且無出流；解析入流量為10×60+0.5×0.1×60²=780 m³。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Assume Q(t)=10+0.1t m³/s for 60 s with no outflow.","failure":"常見誤解：「把水力參數重新校正到量測曲線，就一定能消除任何時間步長造成的數值誤差。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Recalibrating hydraulic parameters always eliminates numerical error caused by the chosen time step.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「時間步長與數值守恆」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Time steps and numerical conservation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-21-k1","title":"時間步長與數值守恆","titleEn":"Time steps and numerical conservation","text":"動態水量模型將連續的入流與出流積分成蓄水變化，有限時間步長會引入離散誤差。若入流在步內快速增加，使用步首值會低估水量；縮短步長通常有助於比較收斂，但不能修正漏掉的水路或錯誤的邊界。","textEn":"A dynamic balance integrates changing inflow and outflow into storage, and finite time steps introduce discretization error. Using the initial inflow underestimates volume during a rising interval.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：把水力參數重新校正到量測曲線，就一定能消除任何時間步長造成的數值誤差。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Recalibrating hydraulic parameters always eliminates numerical error caused by the chosen time step. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「時間步長與數值守恆」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Time steps and numerical conservation\" is correct?","options":["動態水量模型將連續的入流與出流積分成蓄水變化，有限時間步長會引入離散誤差。","把水力參數重新校正到量測曲線，就一定能消除任何時間步長造成的數值誤差。","驗證殘差的平均值是零，就表示模型的每一個預測值都完全準確。"],"optionsEn":["A dynamic balance integrates changing inflow and outflow into storage, and finite time steps introduce discretization error.","Recalibrating hydraulic parameters always eliminates numerical error caused by the chosen time step.","A zero mean validation residual means every individual model prediction is exact."],"answer":0,"explanation":"動態水量模型將連續的入流與出流積分成蓄水變化，有限時間步長會引入離散誤差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A dynamic balance integrates changing inflow and outflow into storage, and finite time steps introduce discretization error. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b300-v15-22","title":"時間步長與數值守恆：定量估算","titleEn":"Time steps and numerical conservation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「時間步長與數值守恆」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Time steps and numerical conservation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設60 s內入流Q(t)=10+0.1t m³/s且無出流；解析入流量為10×60+0.5×0.1×60²=780 m³。單步左矩形法只有600 m³，少算180 m³。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Assume Q(t)=10+0.1t m³/s for 60 s with no outflow. Exact volume is 780 m³. One initial-value rectangular step gives 600 m³, underestimating volume by 180 m³. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：保留相同物理參數，分別用六十秒、三十秒與十五秒步長重算，與解析積分比較而不是只互相比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Keep physical parameters fixed and compare sixty-, thirty- and fifteen-second calculations against the analytical integral.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設60 s內入流Q(t)=10+0.1t m³/s且無出流；解析入流量為10×60+0.5×0.1×60²=780 m³。單步左矩形法只有600 m³，少算180 m³。","textEn":"Assume Q(t)=10+0.1t m³/s for 60 s with no outflow. Exact volume is 780 m³. One initial-value rectangular step gives 600 m³, underestimating volume by 180 m³.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「時間步長與數值守恆」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Time steps and numerical conservation\", which statement holds?","options":["偵測器的真陽性率是百分之九十五，就表示每次警報都有百分之九十五機率是真的。","教學假設60 s內入流Q(t)=10+0.1t m³/s且無出流；解析入流量為10×60+0.5×0.1×60²=780 m³。","節點出現正水量殘差，就一定代表同等流量的管線漏水。"],"optionsEn":["A ninety-five-percent true-positive rate means every alert has a ninety-five-percent chance of being genuine.","Assume Q(t)=10+0.1t m³/s for 60 s with no outflow.","A positive node balance residual always equals the physical leakage flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設60 s內入流Q(t)=10+0.1t m³/s且無出流；解析入流量為10×60+0.5×0.1×60²=780 m³。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Assume Q(t)=10+0.1t m³/s for 60 s with no outflow. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b300-v15-23","title":"時間步長與數值守恆：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Time steps and numerical conservation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「時間步長與數值守恆」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Time steps and numerical conservation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"保留相同物理參數，分別用六十秒、三十秒與十五秒步長重算，與解析積分比較而不是只互相比較。記錄每步蓄水與入出流的守恆差，並檢查事件是否落在步長邊界；對沒有解析解的案例，仍須建立網格或步長收斂證據。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Keep physical parameters fixed and compare sixty-, thirty- and fifteen-second calculations against the analytical integral. Record interval balance residuals and event alignment. When an analytical solution is unavailable, still establish step-size convergence rather than accepting agreement between two coarse simulations. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：手算三十秒與十五秒左矩形法的總入流量，畫出誤差隨步長縮小的變化。再用梯形法處理相同線性入流，說明它為何在此特例得到解析值，但不保證對所有快速變化訊號都無誤差。","observationEn":"Site practice: Calculate thirty- and fifteen-second left-rectangle totals and plot error against step size. Apply the trapezoidal rule to the same linear inflow, explaining why it is exact here without implying exactness for arbitrary rapidly changing signals.","failure":"注意干擾：若直接調整入流係數補償過粗步長，校正值會隨時間解析度改變，失去可轉移性。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Adjusting inflow coefficients to compensate for coarse integration makes calibration depend on time resolution. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"保留相同物理參數，分別用六十秒、三十秒與十五秒步長重算，與解析積分比較而不是只互相比較。記錄每步蓄水與入出流的守恆差，並檢查事件是否落在步長邊界；對沒有解析解的案例，仍須建立網格或步長收斂證據。","textEn":"Keep physical parameters fixed and compare sixty-, thirty- and fifteen-second calculations against the analytical integral. Record interval balance residuals and event alignment. When an analytical solution is unavailable, still establish step-size convergence rather than accepting agreement between two coarse simulations.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"手算三十秒與十五秒左矩形法的總入流量，畫出誤差隨步長縮小的變化。再用梯形法處理相同線性入流，說明它為何在此特例得到解析值，但不保證對所有快速變化訊號都無誤差。","textEn":"Calculate thirty- and fifteen-second left-rectangle totals and plot error against step size. Apply the trapezoidal rule to the same linear inflow, explaining why it is exact here without implying exactness for arbitrary rapidly changing signals.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「時間步長與數值守恆」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Time steps and numerical conservation\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","兩支壓力計讀值相同，就表示它們所在位置的總水頭必定相同。","保留相同物理參數，分別用六十秒、三十秒與十五秒步長重算，與解析積分比較而不是只互相比較。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Equal pressure readings always imply equal total hydraulic head at both locations.","Keep physical parameters fixed and compare sixty-, thirty- and fifteen-second calculations against the analytical integral."],"answer":2,"explanation":"保留相同物理參數，分別用六十秒、三十秒與十五秒步長重算，與解析積分比較而不是只互相比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Keep physical parameters fixed and compare sixty-, thirty- and fifteen-second calculations against the analytical integral. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b300-v15-24","title":"時間步長與數值守恆：失效診斷","titleEn":"Time steps and numerical conservation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「時間步長與數值守恆」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Time steps and numerical conservation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若直接調整入流係數補償過粗步長，校正值會隨時間解析度改變，失去可轉移性。單一時間點的水位吻合也可能掩蓋期間水量誤差，因此驗證應同時檢查軌跡與累積量。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Adjusting inflow coefficients to compensate for coarse integration makes calibration depend on time resolution. Agreement at one water level can conceal interval volume error, so validation should examine both the trajectory and accumulated quantities. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：對已知解析解的合成案例先做數值驗證，再以不同步長比較水量閉合，可避免把演算法誤差當成需要重新校正的水力參數。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Start with synthetic cases having analytical solutions, then compare balance closure across time steps so that numerical error is not absorbed into calibrated hydraulic parameters.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「把水力參數重新校正到量測曲線，就一定能消除任何時間步長造成的數值誤差。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Recalibrating hydraulic parameters always eliminates numerical error caused by the chosen time step.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若直接調整入流係數補償過粗步長，校正值會隨時間解析度改變，失去可轉移性。單一時間點的水位吻合也可能掩蓋期間水量誤差，因此驗證應同時檢查軌跡與累積量。","textEn":"Adjusting inflow coefficients to compensate for coarse integration makes calibration depend on time resolution. Agreement at one water level can conceal interval volume error, so validation should examine both the trajectory and accumulated quantities.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「時間步長與數值守恆」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Time steps and numerical conservation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若直接調整入流係數補償過粗步長，校正值會隨時間解析度改變，失去可轉移性。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","驗證殘差的平均值是零，就表示模型的每一個預測值都完全準確。"],"optionsEn":["Adjusting inflow coefficients to compensate for coarse integration makes calibration depend on time resolution.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","A zero mean validation residual means every individual model prediction is exact."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若直接調整入流係數補償過粗步長，校正值會隨時間解析度改變，失去可轉移性。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Adjusting inflow coefficients to compensate for coarse integration makes calibration depend on time resolution. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b300-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「保留驗證資料與殘差指標」與「狀態估計與資料同化」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Held-out validation and residual metrics\" and \"State estimation and data assimilation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b300-v15-25","title":"保留驗證資料與殘差指標：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Held-out validation and residual metrics: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「保留驗證資料與殘差指標」如何影響水利設施數位孿生的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Held-out validation and residual metrics” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Digital twins for water infrastructure”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"校正資料與驗證資料的分離，是判斷數位孿生能否描述未見工況的重要步驟。平均誤差反映整體偏移，均方根誤差則同時包含偏差與離散程度；正負誤差抵消後的零平均值，不代表預測逐點正確。時間序列若相鄰樣本高度相關，隨機切分會把幾乎相同的事件放進兩邊，使表現過度樂觀。應依完整事件、季節或設備工況分組留出資料，再同時檢查尖峰、低流量與狀態切換的殘差分布，而不只報告一個平均分數。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「保留驗證資料與殘差指標」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Separating calibration and validation data tests whether a twin represents unseen conditions. Mean error describes overall bias, while root-mean-square error includes both bias and scatter; cancelling positive and negative errors does not imply pointwise accuracy. Randomly splitting highly correlated time samples can place nearly identical events in both sets. Hold out complete events, seasons or operating states, and examine peak, low-flow and switching residuals separately instead of reporting only one averaged score. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Held-out validation and residual metrics” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設四個保留樣本的水頭殘差為1、−1、2、−2 m；平均偏差為0 m，但RMSE=√((1²+1²+2²+2²)/4)=1.581 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Assume held-out head residuals of 1, −1, 2 and −2 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「驗證殘差的平均值是零，就表示模型的每一個預測值都完全準確。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A zero mean validation residual means every individual model prediction is exact.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「保留驗證資料與殘差指標」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Held-out validation and residual metrics”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-25-k1","title":"保留驗證資料與殘差指標","titleEn":"Held-out validation and residual metrics","text":"校正資料與驗證資料的分離，是判斷數位孿生能否描述未見工況的重要步驟。平均誤差反映整體偏移，均方根誤差則同時包含偏差與離散程度；正負誤差抵消後的零平均值，不代表預測逐點正確。","textEn":"Separating calibration and validation data tests whether a twin represents unseen conditions. Mean error describes overall bias, while root-mean-square error includes both bias and scatter; cancelling positive and negative errors does not imply pointwise accuracy.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：驗證殘差的平均值是零，就表示模型的每一個預測值都完全準確。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A zero mean validation residual means every individual model prediction is exact. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「保留驗證資料與殘差指標」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Held-out validation and residual metrics\" is correct?","options":["驗證殘差的平均值是零，就表示模型的每一個預測值都完全準確。","校正資料與驗證資料的分離，是判斷數位孿生能否描述未見工況的重要步驟。","資料同化後的不確定度下降，就能證明原本的物理模型完全正確。"],"optionsEn":["A zero mean validation residual means every individual model prediction is exact.","Separating calibration and validation data tests whether a twin represents unseen conditions.","Reduced uncertainty after assimilation proves that the underlying physical model is completely correct."],"answer":1,"explanation":"校正資料與驗證資料的分離，是判斷數位孿生能否描述未見工況的重要步驟。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Separating calibration and validation data tests whether a twin represents unseen conditions. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b300-v15-26","title":"保留驗證資料與殘差指標：定量估算","titleEn":"Held-out validation and residual metrics: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「保留驗證資料與殘差指標」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Held-out validation and residual metrics” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設四個保留樣本的水頭殘差為1、−1、2、−2 m；平均偏差為0 m，但RMSE=√((1²+1²+2²+2²)/4)=1.581 m。此結果僅描述這四筆資料。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Assume held-out head residuals of 1, −1, 2 and −2 m. Mean bias is zero, but RMSE=√((1+1+4+4)/4)=1.581 m. These metrics describe only the four stated samples. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在校正前決定資料分組與驗證指標，避免看過答案才挑選容易的測試區段。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Define data groups and metrics before calibration.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設四個保留樣本的水頭殘差為1、−1、2、−2 m；平均偏差為0 m，但RMSE=√((1²+1²+2²+2²)/4)=1.581 m。此結果僅描述這四筆資料。","textEn":"Assume held-out head residuals of 1, −1, 2 and −2 m. Mean bias is zero, but RMSE=√((1+1+4+4)/4)=1.581 m. These metrics describe only the four stated samples.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「保留驗證資料與殘差指標」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Held-out validation and residual metrics\", which statement holds?","options":["只要數位孿生預測某方案耗能較低，就可以忽略供水限制直接執行。","只要兩條曲線的相關係數最高，就證明兩個感測器已正確同步。","教學假設四個保留樣本的水頭殘差為1、−1、2、−2 m；平均偏差為0 m，但RMSE=√((1²+1²+2²+2²)/4)=1.581 m。"],"optionsEn":["Any strategy predicted to use less energy can be implemented without checking water-service constraints.","Maximum correlation between two curves proves that their sensors are correctly synchronized.","Assume held-out head residuals of 1, −1, 2 and −2 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設四個保留樣本的水頭殘差為1、−1、2、−2 m；平均偏差為0 m，但RMSE=√((1²+1²+2²+2²)/4)=1.581 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Assume held-out head residuals of 1, −1, 2 and −2 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b300-v15-27","title":"保留驗證資料與殘差指標：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Held-out validation and residual metrics: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「保留驗證資料與殘差指標」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Held-out validation and residual metrics” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在校正前決定資料分組與驗證指標，避免看過答案才挑選容易的測試區段。對每個保留事件列出偏差、均方根誤差與最大絕對誤差，並檢查品質旗標及缺值比例；將模型不適用的工況明列，不能直接刪去表現差的資料。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Define data groups and metrics before calibration. For each held-out event, report bias, RMSE and maximum absolute error while checking quality flags and missingness. Identify unsupported operating conditions explicitly instead of removing difficult records after inspecting model performance. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：分別計算四筆殘差的平均絕對誤差與最大絕對誤差，與均方根誤差比較。再加入大量零殘差樣本，觀察平均指標如何下降，並說明為何尖峰誤差與原本兩公尺的失準並未因此改善。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compute mean absolute and maximum absolute error for the four residuals and compare RMSE. Add many zero residuals, observe the averaged metrics decrease, and explain why the original two-metre failures have not improved.","failure":"注意干擾：若在驗證資料上反覆選參數，該資料就已參與模型選擇，不再是獨立檢驗。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Repeated parameter selection on validation records makes them part of model development. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在校正前決定資料分組與驗證指標，避免看過答案才挑選容易的測試區段。對每個保留事件列出偏差、均方根誤差與最大絕對誤差，並檢查品質旗標及缺值比例；將模型不適用的工況明列，不能直接刪去表現差的資料。","textEn":"Define data groups and metrics before calibration. For each held-out event, report bias, RMSE and maximum absolute error while checking quality flags and missingness. Identify unsupported operating conditions explicitly instead of removing difficult records after inspecting model performance.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"分別計算四筆殘差的平均絕對誤差與最大絕對誤差，與均方根誤差比較。再加入大量零殘差樣本，觀察平均指標如何下降，並說明為何尖峰誤差與原本兩公尺的失準並未因此改善。","textEn":"Compute mean absolute and maximum absolute error for the four residuals and compare RMSE. Add many zero residuals, observe the averaged metrics decrease, and explain why the original two-metre failures have not improved.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「保留驗證資料與殘差指標」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Held-out validation and residual metrics\"?","options":["在校正前決定資料分組與驗證指標，避免看過答案才挑選容易的測試區段。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","把同一支感測器的資料複製十份再平均，就能得到十支獨立儀器的準確度。"],"optionsEn":["Define data groups and metrics before calibration.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Copying one sensor record ten times provides the accuracy of ten independent instruments."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在校正前決定資料分組與驗證指標，避免看過答案才挑選容易的測試區段。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Define data groups and metrics before calibration. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b300-v15-28","title":"保留驗證資料與殘差指標：失效診斷","titleEn":"Held-out validation and residual metrics: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「保留驗證資料與殘差指標」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Held-out validation and residual metrics” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若在驗證資料上反覆選參數，該資料就已參與模型選擇，不再是獨立檢驗。將大量平穩時段混入短暫失準事件，也會壓低總體平均誤差，使真正影響決策的少數失敗被稀釋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Repeated parameter selection on validation records makes them part of model development. Large amounts of quiet operation can also dilute short but consequential failures, lowering an overall average while leaving decision-relevant errors unresolved. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：應依完整事件、季節或設備工況分組留出資料，再同時檢查尖峰、低流量與狀態切換的殘差分布，而不只報告一個平均分數。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Hold out complete events, seasons or operating states, and examine peak, low-flow and switching residuals separately instead of reporting only one averaged score.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「驗證殘差的平均值是零，就表示模型的每一個預測值都完全準確。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A zero mean validation residual means every individual model prediction is exact.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若在驗證資料上反覆選參數，該資料就已參與模型選擇，不再是獨立檢驗。將大量平穩時段混入短暫失準事件，也會壓低總體平均誤差，使真正影響決策的少數失敗被稀釋。","textEn":"Repeated parameter selection on validation records makes them part of model development. Large amounts of quiet operation can also dilute short but consequential failures, lowering an overall average while leaving decision-relevant errors unresolved.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「保留驗證資料與殘差指標」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Held-out validation and residual metrics\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若在驗證資料上反覆選參數，該資料就已參與模型選擇，不再是獨立檢驗。","資料同化後的不確定度下降，就能證明原本的物理模型完全正確。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Repeated parameter selection on validation records makes them part of model development.","Reduced uncertainty after assimilation proves that the underlying physical model is completely correct."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若在驗證資料上反覆選參數，該資料就已參與模型選擇，不再是獨立檢驗。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Repeated parameter selection on validation records makes them part of model development. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b300-v15-29","title":"狀態估計與資料同化：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"State estimation and data assimilation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「狀態估計與資料同化」如何影響水利設施數位孿生的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “State estimation and data assimilation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Digital twins for water infrastructure”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"資料同化利用新觀測修正模型內部狀態，並依預測與量測不確定度決定修正幅度。最簡單的純量卡爾曼更新假設線性、無偏且誤差獨立；水池高度可以作為狀態，但實際系統還可能需要需求量、流量與感測器偏移等多個狀態。更新後的不確定度變小，只表示在既定統計模型下資訊增加，不保證物理方程正確。若資料被重複使用或誤差相關性未處理，估計器可能顯示非常自信，卻無法預測下一個真實事件。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「狀態估計與資料同化」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Assimilation updates internal model states using new observations, with the correction governed by prediction and measurement uncertainty. A scalar Kalman update assumes linearity, unbiased independent errors and known variances. Tank level can be a state, although real systems may also require demand, flow and sensor-bias states. Reduced variance means added information within that statistical model, not proof of correct physics. Reused observations or ignored correlations can produce an overconfident estimate that fails on the next event. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “State estimation and data assimilation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學純量案例：預測水位10 m、預測變異數4 m²，觀測14 m、量測變異數1 m²；K=4/(4+1)=0.8，更新水位10+0.8×4=13.2 m，更新變異數0.8 m²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: For a scalar teaching case, predicted level is 10 m with variance 4 m²; observation is 14 m with variance 1 m².","failure":"常見誤解：「資料同化後的不確定度下降，就能證明原本的物理模型完全正確。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Reduced uncertainty after assimilation proves that the underlying physical model is completely correct.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「狀態估計與資料同化」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “State estimation and data assimilation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-29-k1","title":"狀態估計與資料同化","titleEn":"State estimation and data assimilation","text":"資料同化利用新觀測修正模型內部狀態，並依預測與量測不確定度決定修正幅度。最簡單的純量卡爾曼更新假設線性、無偏且誤差獨立；水池高度可以作為狀態，但實際系統還可能需要需求量、流量與感測器偏移等多個狀態。","textEn":"Assimilation updates internal model states using new observations, with the correction governed by prediction and measurement uncertainty. A scalar Kalman update assumes linearity, unbiased independent errors and known variances.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：資料同化後的不確定度下降，就能證明原本的物理模型完全正確。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Reduced uncertainty after assimilation proves that the underlying physical model is completely correct. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「狀態估計與資料同化」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"State estimation and data assimilation\" is correct?","options":["資料同化後的不確定度下降，就能證明原本的物理模型完全正確。","偵測器的真陽性率是百分之九十五，就表示每次警報都有百分之九十五機率是真的。","資料同化利用新觀測修正模型內部狀態，並依預測與量測不確定度決定修正幅度。"],"optionsEn":["Reduced uncertainty after assimilation proves that the underlying physical model is completely correct.","A ninety-five-percent true-positive rate means every alert has a ninety-five-percent chance of being genuine.","Assimilation updates internal model states using new observations, with the correction governed by prediction and measurement uncertainty."],"answer":2,"explanation":"資料同化利用新觀測修正模型內部狀態，並依預測與量測不確定度決定修正幅度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Assimilation updates internal model states using new observations, with the correction governed by prediction and measurement uncertainty. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b300-v15-30","title":"狀態估計與資料同化：定量估算","titleEn":"State estimation and data assimilation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「狀態估計與資料同化」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “State estimation and data assimilation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學純量案例：預測水位10 m、預測變異數4 m²，觀測14 m、量測變異數1 m²；K=4/(4+1)=0.8，更新水位10+0.8×4=13.2 m，更新變異數0.8 m²。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: For a scalar teaching case, predicted level is 10 m with variance 4 m²; observation is 14 m with variance 1 m². Gain K=0.8 gives updated level 13.2 m and variance 0.8 m². Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先核對變異數與標準差沒有混用，再以獨立合成訊號測試更新公式。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check that variances are not confused with standard deviations, then test the update on independent synthetic signals.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學純量案例：預測水位10 m、預測變異數4 m²，觀測14 m、量測變異數1 m²；K=4/(4+1)=0.8，更新水位10+0.8×4=13.2 m，更新變異數0.8 m²。","textEn":"For a scalar teaching case, predicted level is 10 m with variance 4 m²; observation is 14 m with variance 1 m². Gain K=0.8 gives updated level 13.2 m and variance 0.8 m².","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「狀態估計與資料同化」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"State estimation and data assimilation\", which statement holds?","options":["教學純量案例：預測水位10 m、預測變異數4 m²，觀測14 m、量測變異數1 m²。","節點出現正水量殘差，就一定代表同等流量的管線漏水。","兩支壓力計讀值相同，就表示它們所在位置的總水頭必定相同。"],"optionsEn":["For a scalar teaching case, predicted level is 10 m with variance 4 m²; observation is 14 m with variance 1 m².","A positive node balance residual always equals the physical leakage flow.","Equal pressure readings always imply equal total hydraulic head at both locations."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學純量案例：預測水位10 m、預測變異數4 m²，觀測14 m、量測變異數1 m²；K=4/(4+1)=0.8，更新水位10+0.8×4=13.2 m，更新變異數0.8 m²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"For a scalar teaching case, predicted level is 10 m with variance 4 m²; observation is 14 m with variance 1 m². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b300-v15-31","title":"狀態估計與資料同化：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"State estimation and data assimilation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「狀態估計與資料同化」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “State estimation and data assimilation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先核對變異數與標準差沒有混用，再以獨立合成訊號測試更新公式。記錄更新前的創新量與其預測變異數，檢查它是否長期偏離零或呈連續相關；若持續出現同方向偏差，應評估模型或感測器偏移，而不是無限制調大增益。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check that variances are not confused with standard deviations, then test the update on independent synthetic signals. Record innovations and predicted innovation variance, examining persistent bias and serial correlation before attributing improvement to a larger gain or more frequent updates. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把量測變異數從一平方公尺改為九平方公尺，重算增益、更新水位與變異數，說明結果為何更靠近模型預測。再分析同一量測被錯誤重複同化時，估計器會出現哪一種虛假的信心。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change measurement variance from one to nine square metres and recompute gain, level and variance. Explain the increased weight on the prediction, then analyze the false confidence caused by assimilating the same measurement repeatedly.","failure":"注意干擾：同一觀測若在一次更新後又當作新資料重複加入，會讓變異數不合理地縮小。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Reusing the same observation as new evidence shrinks variance incorrectly. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先核對變異數與標準差沒有混用，再以獨立合成訊號測試更新公式。記錄更新前的創新量與其預測變異數，檢查它是否長期偏離零或呈連續相關；若持續出現同方向偏差，應評估模型或感測器偏移，而不是無限制調大增益。","textEn":"Check that variances are not confused with standard deviations, then test the update on independent synthetic signals. Record innovations and predicted innovation variance, examining persistent bias and serial correlation before attributing improvement to a larger gain or more frequent updates.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把量測變異數從一平方公尺改為九平方公尺，重算增益、更新水位與變異數，說明結果為何更靠近模型預測。再分析同一量測被錯誤重複同化時，估計器會出現哪一種虛假的信心。","textEn":"Change measurement variance from one to nine square metres and recompute gain, level and variance. Explain the increased weight on the prediction, then analyze the false confidence caused by assimilating the same measurement repeatedly.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「狀態估計與資料同化」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"State estimation and data assimilation\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","先核對變異數與標準差沒有混用，再以獨立合成訊號測試更新公式。","最佳化程式只回傳一組參數，就證明這組參數已被資料唯一辨識。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Check that variances are not confused with standard deviations, then test the update on independent synthetic signals.","A single parameter vector returned by an optimizer proves unique identification by the data."],"answer":1,"explanation":"先核對變異數與標準差沒有混用，再以獨立合成訊號測試更新公式。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check that variances are not confused with standard deviations, then test the update on independent synthetic signals. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b300-v15-32","title":"狀態估計與資料同化：失效診斷","titleEn":"State estimation and data assimilation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「狀態估計與資料同化」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “State estimation and data assimilation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"同一觀測若在一次更新後又當作新資料重複加入，會讓變異數不合理地縮小。若更新後水位超出物理幾何範圍，簡單截斷也會改變統計分布，必須明確記錄約束處理方式。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Reusing the same observation as new evidence shrinks variance incorrectly. Clipping updated levels to physical bounds also changes their statistical distribution and must be documented as a constraint treatment, not presented as an unchanged unconstrained update. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若資料被重複使用或誤差相關性未處理，估計器可能顯示非常自信，卻無法預測下一個真實事件。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Reused observations or ignored correlations can produce an overconfident estimate that fails on the next event.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「資料同化後的不確定度下降，就能證明原本的物理模型完全正確。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Reduced uncertainty after assimilation proves that the underlying physical model is completely correct.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"同一觀測若在一次更新後又當作新資料重複加入，會讓變異數不合理地縮小。若更新後水位超出物理幾何範圍，簡單截斷也會改變統計分布，必須明確記錄約束處理方式。","textEn":"Reusing the same observation as new evidence shrinks variance incorrectly. Clipping updated levels to physical bounds also changes their statistical distribution and must be documented as a constraint treatment, not presented as an unchanged unconstrained update.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「狀態估計與資料同化」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"State estimation and data assimilation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","偵測器的真陽性率是百分之九十五，就表示每次警報都有百分之九十五機率是真的。","同一觀測若在一次更新後又當作新資料重複加入，會讓變異數不合理地縮小。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A ninety-five-percent true-positive rate means every alert has a ninety-five-percent chance of being genuine.","Reusing the same observation as new evidence shrinks variance incorrectly."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同一觀測若在一次更新後又當作新資料重複加入，會讓變異數不合理地縮小。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Reusing the same observation as new evidence shrinks variance incorrectly. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b300-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「異常警報與基準發生率」與「情境比較與可追溯決策」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Anomaly alerts and base rates\" and \"Scenario comparison and traceable decisions\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b300-v15-33","title":"異常警報與基準發生率：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Anomaly alerts and base rates: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「異常警報與基準發生率」如何影響水利設施數位孿生的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Anomaly alerts and base rates” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Digital twins for water infrastructure”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"異常偵測器的真陽性率與偽陽性率描述不同條件下的分類表現，不能直接解讀成一次警報為真的機率。當實際異常很少，正常情況的少量誤報也可能超過真正事件。評估時必須定義事件的時間窗口、持續條件與標記來源，避免把連續一百筆同一事故當成一百次獨立成功。警報應附帶可檢查的殘差、感測品質與相似事件證據，並在資料分布變動時重新評估，不能因為模型輸出一個高分就省略人工判讀。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「異常警報與基準發生率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"True-positive and false-positive rates condition on different underlying states and do not directly give the probability that an alert is genuine. When anomalies are rare, false alerts from normal conditions can outnumber real events. Define event windows, persistence and labeling evidence, avoiding treatment of repeated samples from one incident as independent successes. Alerts should expose inspectable residuals and data quality, and performance should be reevaluated after distribution changes rather than replacing review with a high model score. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Anomaly alerts and base rates” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設事件基準率0.001、真陽性率0.95、偽陽性率0.01；警報為真機率=0.95×0.001/(0.95×0.001+0.01×0.999)=8.68%，假設這些比例適用於同一母體。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Assume event prevalence 0.001, true-positive rate 0.95 and false-positive rate 0.01.","failure":"常見誤解：「偵測器的真陽性率是百分之九十五，就表示每次警報都有百分之九十五機率是真的。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A ninety-five-percent true-positive rate means every alert has a ninety-five-percent chance of being genuine.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「異常警報與基準發生率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Anomaly alerts and base rates”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-33-k1","title":"異常警報與基準發生率","titleEn":"Anomaly alerts and base rates","text":"異常偵測器的真陽性率與偽陽性率描述不同條件下的分類表現，不能直接解讀成一次警報為真的機率。當實際異常很少，正常情況的少量誤報也可能超過真正事件。","textEn":"True-positive and false-positive rates condition on different underlying states and do not directly give the probability that an alert is genuine. When anomalies are rare, false alerts from normal conditions can outnumber real events.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：偵測器的真陽性率是百分之九十五，就表示每次警報都有百分之九十五機率是真的。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A ninety-five-percent true-positive rate means every alert has a ninety-five-percent chance of being genuine. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「異常警報與基準發生率」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Anomaly alerts and base rates\" is correct?","options":["異常偵測器的真陽性率與偽陽性率描述不同條件下的分類表現，不能直接解讀成一次警報為真的機率。","偵測器的真陽性率是百分之九十五，就表示每次警報都有百分之九十五機率是真的。","只要數位孿生預測某方案耗能較低，就可以忽略供水限制直接執行。"],"optionsEn":["True-positive and false-positive rates condition on different underlying states and do not directly give the probability that an alert is genuine.","A ninety-five-percent true-positive rate means every alert has a ninety-five-percent chance of being genuine.","Any strategy predicted to use less energy can be implemented without checking water-service constraints."],"answer":0,"explanation":"異常偵測器的真陽性率與偽陽性率描述不同條件下的分類表現，不能直接解讀成一次警報為真的機率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"True-positive and false-positive rates condition on different underlying states and do not directly give the probability that an alert is genuine. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b300-v15-34","title":"異常警報與基準發生率：定量估算","titleEn":"Anomaly alerts and base rates: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「異常警報與基準發生率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Anomaly alerts and base rates” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設事件基準率0.001、真陽性率0.95、偽陽性率0.01；警報為真機率=0.95×0.001/(0.95×0.001+0.01×0.999)=8.68%，假設這些比例適用於同一母體。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Assume event prevalence 0.001, true-positive rate 0.95 and false-positive rate 0.01. Alert precision is 0.00095/(0.00095+0.00999)=8.68%, provided all rates apply to the same population. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：使用包含正常時段的獨立事件集建立混淆矩陣，列出每種工況的事件基準率。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build confusion matrices from independent event sets including normal operation, with prevalence by operating state.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設事件基準率0.001、真陽性率0.95、偽陽性率0.01；警報為真機率=0.95×0.001/(0.95×0.001+0.01×0.999)=8.68%，假設這些比例適用於同一母體。","textEn":"Assume event prevalence 0.001, true-positive rate 0.95 and false-positive rate 0.01. Alert precision is 0.00095/(0.00095+0.00999)=8.68%, provided all rates apply to the same population.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「異常警報與基準發生率」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Anomaly alerts and base rates\", which statement holds?","options":["只要兩條曲線的相關係數最高，就證明兩個感測器已正確同步。","教學假設事件基準率0.001、真陽性率0.95、偽陽性率0.01。","把同一支感測器的資料複製十份再平均，就能得到十支獨立儀器的準確度。"],"optionsEn":["Maximum correlation between two curves proves that their sensors are correctly synchronized.","Assume event prevalence 0.001, true-positive rate 0.95 and false-positive rate 0.01.","Copying one sensor record ten times provides the accuracy of ten independent instruments."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設事件基準率0.001、真陽性率0.95、偽陽性率0.01；警報為真機率=0.95×0.001/(0.95×0.001+0.01×0.999)=8.68%，假設這些比例適用於同一母體。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Assume event prevalence 0.001, true-positive rate 0.95 and false-positive rate 0.01. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b300-v15-35","title":"異常警報與基準發生率：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Anomaly alerts and base rates: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「異常警報與基準發生率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Anomaly alerts and base rates” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"使用包含正常時段的獨立事件集建立混淆矩陣，列出每種工況的事件基準率。將警報合併規則與人工複核結果保留，分開計算事件層級與樣本層級指標，並追蹤漏報及誤報的後續處置，不能只蒐集成功警報作成績單。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build confusion matrices from independent event sets including normal operation, with prevalence by operating state. Preserve alert-grouping rules and reviewed outcomes, separating event-level from sample-level metrics and tracking missed incidents as well as false alarms instead of collecting only successful alerts. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以十萬個獨立教學事件建表，計算預期真警報與假警報數量。再把基準率提高十倍而保持兩種分類率不變，重算警報可信度，說明相同分類器為何會在不同母體呈現不同的使用價值。","observationEn":"Site practice: Tabulate expected true and false alerts across one hundred thousand independent teaching events. Increase prevalence tenfold while holding classification rates fixed, then recompute precision and explain why the same classifier has different practical value in another population.","failure":"注意干擾：若只在預先挑選的異常樣本上展示高命中率，就無法知道正常運轉會產生多少誤報。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: High hit rates on preselected abnormal records say nothing about false alerts during normal operation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"使用包含正常時段的獨立事件集建立混淆矩陣，列出每種工況的事件基準率。將警報合併規則與人工複核結果保留，分開計算事件層級與樣本層級指標，並追蹤漏報及誤報的後續處置，不能只蒐集成功警報作成績單。","textEn":"Build confusion matrices from independent event sets including normal operation, with prevalence by operating state. Preserve alert-grouping rules and reviewed outcomes, separating event-level from sample-level metrics and tracking missed incidents as well as false alarms instead of collecting only successful alerts.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以十萬個獨立教學事件建表，計算預期真警報與假警報數量。再把基準率提高十倍而保持兩種分類率不變，重算警報可信度，說明相同分類器為何會在不同母體呈現不同的使用價值。","textEn":"Tabulate expected true and false alerts across one hundred thousand independent teaching events. Increase prevalence tenfold while holding classification rates fixed, then recompute precision and explain why the same classifier has different practical value in another population.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「異常警報與基準發生率」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Anomaly alerts and base rates\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","把水力參數重新校正到量測曲線，就一定能消除任何時間步長造成的數值誤差。","使用包含正常時段的獨立事件集建立混淆矩陣，列出每種工況的事件基準率。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Recalibrating hydraulic parameters always eliminates numerical error caused by the chosen time step.","Build confusion matrices from independent event sets including normal operation, with prevalence by operating state."],"answer":2,"explanation":"使用包含正常時段的獨立事件集建立混淆矩陣，列出每種工況的事件基準率。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build confusion matrices from independent event sets including normal operation, with prevalence by operating state. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b300-v15-36","title":"異常警報與基準發生率：失效診斷","titleEn":"Anomaly alerts and base rates: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「異常警報與基準發生率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Anomaly alerts and base rates” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只在預先挑選的異常樣本上展示高命中率，就無法知道正常運轉會產生多少誤報。模型上線後需求型態或儀器更換也可能改變基準率與誤差分布，使過去的警報可信度不再適用。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"High hit rates on preselected abnormal records say nothing about false alerts during normal operation. Changing demand patterns or instruments can alter prevalence and error distributions, invalidating a previously measured alert precision. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：警報應附帶可檢查的殘差、感測品質與相似事件證據，並在資料分布變動時重新評估，不能因為模型輸出一個高分就省略人工判讀。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Alerts should expose inspectable residuals and data quality, and performance should be reevaluated after distribution changes rather than replacing review with a high model score.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「偵測器的真陽性率是百分之九十五，就表示每次警報都有百分之九十五機率是真的。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A ninety-five-percent true-positive rate means every alert has a ninety-five-percent chance of being genuine.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只在預先挑選的異常樣本上展示高命中率，就無法知道正常運轉會產生多少誤報。模型上線後需求型態或儀器更換也可能改變基準率與誤差分布，使過去的警報可信度不再適用。","textEn":"High hit rates on preselected abnormal records say nothing about false alerts during normal operation. Changing demand patterns or instruments can alter prevalence and error distributions, invalidating a previously measured alert precision.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「異常警報與基準發生率」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Anomaly alerts and base rates\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若只在預先挑選的異常樣本上展示高命中率，就無法知道正常運轉會產生多少誤報。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","只要數位孿生預測某方案耗能較低，就可以忽略供水限制直接執行。"],"optionsEn":["High hit rates on preselected abnormal records say nothing about false alerts during normal operation.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Any strategy predicted to use less energy can be implemented without checking water-service constraints."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若只在預先挑選的異常樣本上展示高命中率，就無法知道正常運轉會產生多少誤報。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"High hit rates on preselected abnormal records say nothing about false alerts during normal operation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b300-v15-37","title":"情境比較與可追溯決策：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Scenario comparison and traceable decisions: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「情境比較與可追溯決策」如何影響水利設施數位孿生的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Scenario comparison and traceable decisions” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Digital twins for water infrastructure”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"數位孿生的情境比較應固定需求、邊界及評估期間，才能把節能差異歸因於所比較的策略。單位供水能耗只是其中一項指標，仍需同時滿足水位、水壓、水質與設備限制；較低能耗若伴隨供水不足，不能視為等效服務下的改善。每次分析應保存模型版本、資料時間範圍、參數、假設和人工審查結果，使未來能重播同一情境。生成式助教可協助整理證據與解釋差異，但其文字結論不能代替可執行模型輸出或現場授權程序。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「情境比較與可追溯決策」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Scenario comparison holds demand, boundaries and assessment duration fixed so that energy differences can be attributed to the proposed strategy. Specific energy is only one metric alongside level, pressure, quality and equipment constraints; lower energy with unmet demand is not equivalent service improvement. Preserve model version, data period, parameters, assumptions and reviewed conclusions for reproducible replay. A generative tutor can organize evidence and explain differences, but its prose does not replace executable model results or authorized operating procedures. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Scenario comparison and traceable decisions” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設兩方案均供水1000 m³且均滿足相同限制，耗能分別200與180 kWh；單位能耗0.20與0.18 kWh/m³，節能率(200−180)/200=10%，未含價格差與設備磨耗。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Assume both strategies supply 1000 m³ and satisfy identical constraints, using 200 and 180 kWh.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要數位孿生預測某方案耗能較低，就可以忽略供水限制直接執行。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Any strategy predicted to use less energy can be implemented without checking water-service constraints.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「情境比較與可追溯決策」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Scenario comparison and traceable decisions”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-37-k1","title":"情境比較與可追溯決策","titleEn":"Scenario comparison and traceable decisions","text":"數位孿生的情境比較應固定需求、邊界及評估期間，才能把節能差異歸因於所比較的策略。單位供水能耗只是其中一項指標，仍需同時滿足水位、水壓、水質與設備限制；較低能耗若伴隨供水不足，不能視為等效服務下的改善。","textEn":"Scenario comparison holds demand, boundaries and assessment duration fixed so that energy differences can be attributed to the proposed strategy. Specific energy is only one metric alongside level, pressure, quality and equipment constraints; lower energy with unmet demand is not equivalent service improvement.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要數位孿生預測某方案耗能較低，就可以忽略供水限制直接執行。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Any strategy predicted to use less energy can be implemented without checking water-service constraints. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「情境比較與可追溯決策」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Scenario comparison and traceable decisions\" is correct?","options":["只要數位孿生預測某方案耗能較低，就可以忽略供水限制直接執行。","數位孿生的情境比較應固定需求、邊界及評估期間，才能把節能差異歸因於所比較的策略。","節點出現正水量殘差，就一定代表同等流量的管線漏水。"],"optionsEn":["Any strategy predicted to use less energy can be implemented without checking water-service constraints.","Scenario comparison holds demand, boundaries and assessment duration fixed so that energy differences can be attributed to the proposed strategy.","A positive node balance residual always equals the physical leakage flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"數位孿生的情境比較應固定需求、邊界及評估期間，才能把節能差異歸因於所比較的策略。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Scenario comparison holds demand, boundaries and assessment duration fixed so that energy differences can be attributed to the proposed strategy. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b300-v15-38","title":"情境比較與可追溯決策：定量估算","titleEn":"Scenario comparison and traceable decisions: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「情境比較與可追溯決策」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Scenario comparison and traceable decisions” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設兩方案均供水1000 m³且均滿足相同限制，耗能分別200與180 kWh；單位能耗0.20與0.18 kWh/m³，節能率(200−180)/200=10%，未含價格差與設備磨耗。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Assume both strategies supply 1000 m³ and satisfy identical constraints, using 200 and 180 kWh. Specific energy is 0.20 and 0.18 kWh/m³, a 10% reduction excluding tariff differences and equipment wear. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先對照兩方案的供水量、服務品質與邊界條件，再檢查能耗計算是否包含同一組設備。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare supplied volume, service quality and boundaries before checking that energy includes the same equipment.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設兩方案均供水1000 m³且均滿足相同限制，耗能分別200與180 kWh；單位能耗0.20與0.18 kWh/m³，節能率(200−180)/200=10%，未含價格差與設備磨耗。","textEn":"Assume both strategies supply 1000 m³ and satisfy identical constraints, using 200 and 180 kWh. Specific energy is 0.20 and 0.18 kWh/m³, a 10% reduction excluding tariff differences and equipment wear.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「情境比較與可追溯決策」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Scenario comparison and traceable decisions\", which statement holds?","options":["兩支壓力計讀值相同，就表示它們所在位置的總水頭必定相同。","最佳化程式只回傳一組參數，就證明這組參數已被資料唯一辨識。","教學假設兩方案均供水1000 m³且均滿足相同限制，耗能分別200與180 kWh。"],"optionsEn":["Equal pressure readings always imply equal total hydraulic head at both locations.","A single parameter vector returned by an optimizer proves unique identification by the data.","Assume both strategies supply 1000 m³ and satisfy identical constraints, using 200 and 180 kWh."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設兩方案均供水1000 m³且均滿足相同限制，耗能分別200與180 kWh；單位能耗0.20與0.18 kWh/m³，節能率(200−180)/200=10%，未含價格差與設備磨耗。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Assume both strategies supply 1000 m³ and satisfy identical constraints, using 200 and 180 kWh. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b300-v15-39","title":"情境比較與可追溯決策：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Scenario comparison and traceable decisions: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「情境比較與可追溯決策」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Scenario comparison and traceable decisions” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先對照兩方案的供水量、服務品質與邊界條件，再檢查能耗計算是否包含同一組設備。用資料與模型雜湊記錄可重播版本，另列需求及參數敏感度，最後把待現場驗證的假設與已被量測支持的結論分開，避免把模擬排名直接當成操作命令。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare supplied volume, service quality and boundaries before checking that energy includes the same equipment. Record replayable data and model hashes, evaluate demand sensitivity, and separate assumptions needing field confirmation from supported conclusions before converting a scenario ranking into an operational decision. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：建立兩方案比較表，包含供水量、能耗、單位能耗及限制是否滿足，再把其中一方案供水量減少一成。重算指標並說明為何原先節能結論需要重新判讀，最後列出第三人重播分析所需的最小檔案清單。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare volume, energy, specific energy and constraint compliance, then reduce the delivery of one strategy by ten percent. Recalculate and reconsider the claimed improvement, listing the minimum files another reviewer needs to reproduce the analysis.","failure":"注意干擾：若兩方案使用不同需求總量或電價期間，較低帳單不必然表示較高能源效率。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Different demands or tariff periods make lower cost an unreliable indicator of greater energy efficiency. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先對照兩方案的供水量、服務品質與邊界條件，再檢查能耗計算是否包含同一組設備。用資料與模型雜湊記錄可重播版本，另列需求及參數敏感度，最後把待現場驗證的假設與已被量測支持的結論分開，避免把模擬排名直接當成操作命令。","textEn":"Compare supplied volume, service quality and boundaries before checking that energy includes the same equipment. Record replayable data and model hashes, evaluate demand sensitivity, and separate assumptions needing field confirmation from supported conclusions before converting a scenario ranking into an operational decision.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"建立兩方案比較表，包含供水量、能耗、單位能耗及限制是否滿足，再把其中一方案供水量減少一成。重算指標並說明為何原先節能結論需要重新判讀，最後列出第三人重播分析所需的最小檔案清單。","textEn":"Compare volume, energy, specific energy and constraint compliance, then reduce the delivery of one strategy by ten percent. Recalculate and reconsider the claimed improvement, listing the minimum files another reviewer needs to reproduce the analysis.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「情境比較與可追溯決策」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Scenario comparison and traceable decisions\"?","options":["先對照兩方案的供水量、服務品質與邊界條件，再檢查能耗計算是否包含同一組設備。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","驗證殘差的平均值是零，就表示模型的每一個預測值都完全準確。"],"optionsEn":["Compare supplied volume, service quality and boundaries before checking that energy includes the same equipment.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A zero mean validation residual means every individual model prediction is exact."],"answer":0,"explanation":"先對照兩方案的供水量、服務品質與邊界條件，再檢查能耗計算是否包含同一組設備。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare supplied volume, service quality and boundaries before checking that energy includes the same equipment. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b300-v15-40","title":"情境比較與可追溯決策：失效診斷","titleEn":"Scenario comparison and traceable decisions: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"prerequisiteIds":["b300-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「情境比較與可追溯決策」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Scenario comparison and traceable decisions” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若兩方案使用不同需求總量或電價期間，較低帳單不必然表示較高能源效率。缺少版本與輸入紀錄的漂亮圖表也無法重現，因此不能在條件已改變後沿用舊排名而不重新計算。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Different demands or tariff periods make lower cost an unreliable indicator of greater energy efficiency. Attractive plots without versioned inputs cannot be reproduced, and old rankings should not be reused after conditions change without recalculation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：生成式助教可協助整理證據與解釋差異，但其文字結論不能代替可執行模型輸出或現場授權程序。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A generative tutor can organize evidence and explain differences, but its prose does not replace executable model results or authorized operating procedures.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要數位孿生預測某方案耗能較低，就可以忽略供水限制直接執行。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Any strategy predicted to use less energy can be implemented without checking water-service constraints.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b300-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若兩方案使用不同需求總量或電價期間，較低帳單不必然表示較高能源效率。缺少版本與輸入紀錄的漂亮圖表也無法重現，因此不能在條件已改變後沿用舊排名而不重新計算。","textEn":"Different demands or tariff periods make lower cost an unreliable indicator of greater energy efficiency. Attractive plots without versioned inputs cannot be reproduced, and old rankings should not be reused after conditions change without recalculation.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]},{"id":"b300-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「情境比較與可追溯決策」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Scenario comparison and traceable decisions\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","若兩方案使用不同需求總量或電價期間，較低帳單不必然表示較高能源效率。","節點出現正水量殘差，就一定代表同等流量的管線漏水。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Different demands or tariff periods make lower cost an unreliable indicator of greater energy efficiency.","A positive node balance residual always equals the physical leakage flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若兩方案使用不同需求總量或電價期間，較低帳單不必然表示較高能源效率。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Different demands or tariff periods make lower cost an unreliable indicator of greater energy efficiency. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-epanet-model","v15s-nist-digital-twin-credibility","v15s-pub-changi-twin-2022"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
